{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread","id":899114,"title":"Exalted Forum Introduction Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-25T10:39:24-07:00","id":899114,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Exalted Forum Introduction Thread","content":"This thread is for introducing ourselves to the forum at large, sharing a bit, and helping this place feel more like a community. I'll start.<br /> <br /> I'm Totentanz. I'm a sysadmin/devops guy living in Texas. I've played RPGs for about twenty years, with a majority of that spent on various DnD versions and White Wolf games. I bought my first Exalted book back in 2003, but didn't actually play the game until around the release of <i>Glories of the Most High</i>. Since then, I've been an off and on contributor to the forum.<br /> <br /> If you're new, welcome! Please introduce yourself. We don't bite...often. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":". 05-25-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:45:57-07:00","id":899125,"title":"","content":"Huh. Okay. Tot's doing the intro thread. Sure. What the hell. (Who are you and what've you done with Tot?)<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, I'm Jetstream. I'm a paper pusher for the Texas State Government. I've been an RPG nerd for... oh... I'mma call it 15 years now, I think that's about when someone got me into Vampire and Demon. I got my first Exalted book in 2001 or 2002, can't recall, but I didn't play anything at all until 2003 when I moved and joined a group. Tot's group, in fact. We still game together. Didn't actually play Exalted until the game we started in... either late 2009 or early 2010. The game I was running, in fact. I'm sporadic on the forums in general.<br /> <br /> Hi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:48:36-07:00","id":899131,"title":"","content":"(I would say share whatever you want to share, nothing is required except courtesy. Introduce whatever you want people to know)<br /> <br /> I'm The Unsung Hero. I work at Costco Wholesale Corporate Office in Washington and do 90% of my forum reading at work, because oddly enough it helps me focus. I've been doing tabletop RPGs for 21 years (mostly D&amp;D) and I've been into Exalted since 2003 (actually this feels a lot like Totentanz's post). I've only been active on the forums since 2012 or so (whenever Shards of the Exalted Dream released) and I've become extra involved since 3E released.<br /> <br /> I am probably best known for my homebrew work on Artifacts, which is linked in my signature. I don't always have lots of free time, but I do like to help people with game stuff (Design, philosophy, whatever) when I am available.<br /> <br /> Be welcome to our community, and count yourself among our number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 05-25-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:54:46-07:00","id":899141,"title":"","content":"Are we obligated to tell everyone where we live and work? Because I'm not going to.<br /> <br /> Hi, I'm Erinys. A decades-long Werewolf: the Apocalypse fan, I've been interested in Exalted since 1st Edition but have never had a chance to play any RPGs offline (except occasionally at a convention). I came for the Prehistory of the WoD, and stayed for the awesome setting. My first exposure to RPGs were actually D&amp;D and the Hero Quest board game, but I don't care for either (except Planescape). On the earlier WW forum and on ShadownEssence I used to be Erinye. In some other fandoms I call myself Faelivrin, Arcades Sabboth, and Vaevictis Asmadi (named for a character, not a philosophical statement!)<br /> <br /> I love Infernals* and I'm not ashamed of it. Solars are my second-favorite Exalted, but I also dig Dragon Kings and non-Bronze Sidereals. I express strong opinions and ask weird questions. I'm fascinated by setting fluff, but don't really understand mechanics, and there are gaps in my knowledge because I don't have many Exalted books, have not yet read most of the ones I do have, and relied a lot on the internet to learn about the setting. I know almost nothing about 3rd Edition or Essence.<br /> <br /> My interests swing between Exalted and various other subjects**, so I leave this forum for months at a time, and then act confused when I wander back in. When I'm away I read fantasy and scifi and actual science, fiddle with GURPS, work for a nonprofit, and try to make the real world a little better place. I WISH I had time and people to play this game.<br /> <br /> *Not the rape parts!<br /> <br /> **Real science, various science fiction, Middle-Earth+Arda, WTA and some other cWoD games, Planescape, various fantasy novels, more fantasy, gardening, social justice bard-ing, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been told my signature reads like it's supposed to be a joke, but actually it's 100% serious. I am very literal-minded. I really really don't know how to &quot;read between the lines&quot; and I have trouble communicating without being misinterpreted. Also tend to misinterpret others' posts, and I very often miss sarcasm. I promise it's always accidental and not me being a jerk. Usually I don't realize it, even after I do it. So if it looks like I &quot;implied&quot; something in a post... I almost certainly didn't. (The very few times I try to imply anything, I generally fail hard.) Please please don't ever read implications into what I write. If I'm trying to be funny or sarcastic, it'll probably be obvious (and bad) because I suck at humor and subtlety.<br /> <br /> If I'm rude it is also a mistake, and if I don't edit my post you can assume I didn't realize I did it. I accept gentle, nonjudgmental, PRIVATE MESSAGE corrections for huge social gaffes, but otherwise just give me the benefit of the doubt, OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-12-2021, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:10:15-07:00","id":899158,"title":"","content":"It feels weird saying &quot;Hi, I'm Foxcalibur&quot; when everyone can clearly see my name is Foxcalibur. Makes me feel like this is a support group and everyone should be all, &quot;Hi, Foxcalibur...&quot;<br /> <br /> Anywho, I'm Foxy. I've been roleplaying since I was maybe 8 and started telling my friends make-believe had rules, and no you can't all be Michelangelo at the same time, and April should have some agency, dammit! I've been a GM/ST way more than a player and mostly like it that way, and am currently running Werewolf: the Forsaken and Changeling: the Lost in a shared near-future setting called The Edge of Everything, which I tried to make really grim only to have the universe out-grim me with Donald Trump: Possible President. Werewolf is about to finish its second season, at which point I'll make my triumphant return to <b>EXALTED, BOYEEEEE! WUT-WUT?!</b> <br /> <br /> I prefer talking about fluff to talking about crunch, and I'm heavily, aggressively narrativist. I'm also a bit of an iconoclast about games. NWoD is way better than oWoD (except for Wraith/Orpheus, which are better than Geist.) 4th Edition is objectively the only good D&amp;D. <br /> <br /> I worked for CCP back when the WoD MMO was a &quot;thing,&quot; but I was never a big insider with the White Wolf crowd. I'm doin' okay as a freelance copywriter. <br /> <br /> Ol' Foxy enjoys pro wrestling and is an unabashed Social Justice Warrior, which is a term we should wear with pride because it sounds fucking awesome. If you see the gamertag or online handle Foxcalibur anywhere, it's almost certainly me. You can tell because he'll tend to go on.<br /> <br /> I was born in a log cabin I helped my father build-- <br /> <br /> Too long? Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:25:22-07:00","id":899178,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm wonderandawe. I'm best know for my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/482675-hero-quest\">crazy Shogunate Sidereal Quest</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/860469-florida-man-is-a-sidereal\">silly</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/792780-drunk-exalted-history\">humor threads</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/673199-priesthood-in-exalted\">occasional</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/843181-exalted-inspiration-weirdest-war-tatics-that-worked\">clickbait</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/892605-ex3-the-wyld-hunt-arrests-but-not-kills-anathema\">threads</a>. My three favorite splats are Sidereals, Dragonblooded, Solars, in that order. Homebrew and other crunchy mechanics aren't my strong suit, but like Winnie-the-Pooh, I'm stuffed with fluff. I got a few setting ideas, I've been slowly (very slowly) fleshing out. You can find them on <a href=\"https://acidspiders.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">my blog</a>.<br /> <br /> I've played/run a bunch of Classic World of Darkness, new World of Darkness, Pathfinder, FATE, Savage Words and various indie games like Dogs in the Vineyard, Mouse Guard, Diaspora, Fiasco, and Primetime Adventures. I found Exalted when I started grad school. It was around the time Dreams of the First Age came out. I came for the crazy magitech and stayed for the godly politics.<br /> <br /> I'm a telecommuting Database Monkey, so this forum has replaced my water cooler talk I'd get at work. Thankfully less football, kids, and church and more anthropological debates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-27-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:26:24-07:00","id":899180,"title":"","content":"Salutations! I go by the handle Octopoid, because I am an octopus (also a liar). I've been involved with RPGs in general since I was introduced to Advanced Dungeons and Dragons WAY back in 1988-1989. I have played White Wolf, D&amp;D, Shadowrun, Fate, Warhammer Fantasy Role-Play, Warhammer 40K RP, Pathfinder, Star Wars... you name it, odds are I've played at least a session. I've been involved with Exalted since its initial, First Edition release and have played extensively throughout all three editions. I work in higher education administration and live in Seattle. I have a 'blog about Exalted stuff (<a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/</a>), upon which anyone is welcome to comment. I have occasionally been a toxic voice on the forums, but I'm struggling hard to be a more positive and reassuring voice. If I ever say something offensive, rude, oblivious, or just plain stupid, please feel free to politely draw it to my attention, and I will blush and hide behind my tentacles. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:36:15-07:00","id":899197,"title":"","content":"Hello, my handle of Saur Ops Specialist is a terrible pun. I tend to do things like that.<br /> <br /> Where I started playing tabletop games is debatable. The Milton-Bradley/Games Workshop collaboration of HeroQuest, aka Warhammer FRP In a Box, could be said to be my first experience, but in terms of games utilizing primarily just books, it was Shadowrun, then in its second edition. though the first book I bought, Paranormal Animals of North America, was older than that. I have books from all five editions of it, but burned out on it after all of the wait what contained in Running Wild. Still like BattleTech and its attendant RPG component, though. I quit D&amp;D before 3.5 came out; it just isn't something I can wrap my head around anymore, in terms of character types.<br /> <br /> I put a cautious foot in WW;s stuff back in 1996 when Kindred: the Embraced was on TV. I promptly switched to Werewolf when I saw the Rokea and Mokole in the player's guide. I got on Exalted in the first edition, and got hooked on Scavenger Sons and the encouragement to make up places and just put them anywhere you felt like it. I have most of both editions, and my favorite Exalted tend to follow from Werewolf, which also gives me some interest in Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> I mostly played first edition, and mostly acted as an ST for 2nd edition. I wouldn't recommend playing 2e. I'm trying to get a grasp on all of the Charms from EX3 to act in either capacity.<br /> <br /> My online name for the White Wolf forums used to be Adamant Siaka, with A_O/Alienated One preceding it on the very, very old version of the forums. I am also Dinosaur on the Freedom Stone Forums, where you can find stories that I wrote nearly a decade ago and some concepts of which I am planning on rewriting for EX3. Predictably enough, I am also SaurOps on the GItP forums, and less obviously, Poisson Resistance on rpg.net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:01:46-07:00","id":899229,"title":"","content":"Hello potential newbies. I'm Kyman, but I also respond to Ky.<br /> <br /> I'm an aspiring writer in Washington, but my day job is selling bees (family business) and it puts me behind a desk for a good portion of the day.<br /> <br /> I've done a lot of roleplaying. D&amp;D 3.5, Pathfinder, 4th Edition, 5th Edition, <i>so many FATE hacks</i>, several metric asstons of Freeform Forum Roleplaying...<br /> <br /> Ran a couple Scion 1E games. The setting and ideas are fine but if you want to play Scion I recommend waiting for the new Edition to hit, or look up one of the many homebrew erratas since Scion 1E unmodified is... Well... You know how people say that 2E Exalted was borked? That shit ain't got nothing on Scion 1E.<br /> <br /> Got into Exalted in Second Edition. My memory's a bit hazy, but I <i>want</i> to say that it was before Infernals hit? It was certainly before the major 2.5 overhaul in the Scroll of Errata, Merchants of Jade, or Shards were released.<br /> <br /> Played a couple of 2E games... Then Ex3 hit and I love it to pieces. Mostly I pop into threads and make observations, and I occasionally have moments where I post things that aren't half as clever or insightful as I may think they are. I don't claim to be an expert on anything aside from writing, and have negative levels of understanding on mechanical balance. That's why I preface a lot of my feedback about homebrew (which I have no confidence in doing myself) with what I feel when reading it rather than any actual critique of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Also, as a note: I try to recognize that taste is odd, and different, and I try to disagree politely rather than dislike someone personally. That being said, I can get passionate. If I edge into jerk or jackass territory, give me a gentle note and I'll probably back off. Just &quot;Hey dude, don't be a jerk about it&quot; usually snaps me out of whatever I'm in.<br /> <br /> Edit: My posts can be full of tl;dr and I can ramble. If my intro weren't obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-25-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:14:43-07:00","id":899243,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I'm Kell Tamer. Been gaming for almost 20 years now in tabletop games. I started with DnD and just kinda devolved from there. I've played a bit of FATE, obviously DnD, 3e, 5e, and Pathfinder. I tried Scion before Exalted. Played some nWoD before I tried oWoD. I have also gotten my hands dirty with Aberrant. I got into Exalted near the end of second edition (a little bit before Shards came out.) I am known among my group as the guy to go to when a rule needs referencing because in the few months from when I started to when that game ended, I devoured everything 2e and 2.5. <br /> <br /> My favorite splats are Dragon Blooded, Lunars, and then probably Infernals. Solars are the one I like least, yet I have played most. <br /> <br /> I try not to cause any conflicts on the forums as mostly I'm a lurker, but occasionally something piques my interest enough to chime in. <br /> <br /> My current schtick in games is small children doing absurdly superhuman things. Usually involving figuring out which mountains make the best ballistics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:23:00-07:00","id":899250,"title":"","content":"Hi. I've been playing tabletop for somewhere approaching 4 years, but I really enjoy it. Came late to the hobby, and have only really come to Exalted since the advent of 3rd edition. I like Solars since that's all I have experience with, but I am very interested by the concept of Sidereals, the ubiquity of the Dragon-Blooded and the potential for Lunar Exalted, though I am a bit dismayed by the lack of any more info on those things.<br /> <br /> I game-master a lot but my girlfriend and my other friends occasionally run games where I play. I love playing social characters and sorcerer types, especially some combination of those two things.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in homebrewing since that seems the chief way to get new content in this edition, but I am very uncertain of how to do stuff like designing evocations without stepping on the toes of charms or doing things that are imbalanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:23:21-07:00","id":899251,"title":"","content":"Hey, AnubisXy here, obviously.<br /> <br /> I've been playing White Wolf games since the early 90's (I got sucked in during the goth period and the &quot;mature games for mature minds&quot; label). I had a few friends who playtested the original Exalted, and was buddies with a couple of authors for 1st and 2nd edition, so i've had my head in the door for awhile. I enjoy running games with small goals and then having things slowly grow over time until everything is completely over-the-top by the end of a campaign.<br /> <br /> I love Abyssals and Infernals (I guess I never did grow out of my goth phase) and am looking forward to Exigents.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm working as an over the road truck driver, so it makes gaming in person difficult at best.<br /> <br /> Whenever I come across a post I disagree with, I try and find at least one element or idea in there that I can agree with. It helps to keep me from being overly aggressive and confrontational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:36:02-07:00","id":899265,"title":"","content":"Hi! I'm Omicron. I'm French and a 25-years old student and aspiring writer. I got into Exalted at the tail end of 2e, although I was into White Wolf games for a while before that (Vampire: the Requiem is one of my first loves). I've loved Ex3 since the first concepts of it were put forward, and even did some playtesting. I run online because it's hard to find Exalted players where I live. <br /> <br /> I write stuff. Lots of stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:49:54-07:00","id":899283,"title":"","content":"I'm Crumplepunch. I live alone in a remote part of the UK with a lot of books and a lot of time. I'm basically a Gothic horror novel villain who has discovered the internet. Sometimes I write things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:51:10-07:00","id":899286,"title":"","content":"I'm Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:56:05-07:00","id":899292,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Noodle. I'm a social worker (disability services) living in the Seattle area, with a background in Political Theory and Macroeconomics. I've been playing tabletop RPGs for about a decade, and got into Exalted about the time Infernals released. <br /> <br /> My favorite Exalts are the Sidereals and Infernals and I'm pretty stoked for Exigents and Getimians. I'm usually my group's ST/GM, and have developed a bit of a reputation as a sadistic ST (though my group keeps asking me to run games for them, so if that's true they're masochists). I also do a fair bit of homebrew (usually for said games), but I hardly ever post anything, since it seems that next to no-one here would appreciate my killer labyrinthine First Age bomb shelters and hyper-synergistic DB death squads. Since homebrew is basically the only reason I come here anymore, I don't really post much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:57:35-07:00","id":899294,"title":"","content":"I'm Colin Fredericks - which is my actual real name!<br /> <br /> I'm in my late 30s. I'm from Vermont originally, but these days I live near Boston and help professors create online courses for my day job. Exalted is tied for my #1 favorite game ever with Mage.<br /> <br /> My big hobby is actually writing RPGs. I write unofficial Ex3 characters and settings at a blog called <a href=\"http://strangercreations.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stranger Creations</a>. I've been writing games since 1995, when I was in high school and wrote a 150-page supplement for Valence 1st Edition. My biggest project recently was <a href=\"http://suffadv.wikidot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sufficiently Advanced</a>, a diceless, high-powered, hard sci-fi game. I've also written the <a href=\"http://console.wikidot.com/start\" target=\"_blank\">Console</a> series, which is a set of Final Fantasy parody games.<br /> <br /> I enjoy martial arts (mostly karate and tai chi), video games (on my Nth playthrough of <i>Symphony of the Night</i>), fantasy and sci-fi books (currently on <i>The Fifth Season</i> by Jemisin), and petting every animal ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:43:32-07:00","id":899347,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I'm Keichiokami and I live in sunny San Diego. I am currently working at a Bar/Bistro/Chocolate Factory shop called Eclipse Chocolate. I am going to school part time for Sociology and I am semster away from two Associates Degrees. I am deeply involved in my gaming and LARP community here in San Diego and I have been into Exalted since 1st Edition. I used to frequent the forums on the old WW site, so I have been on the Official Exalted Forums since they started. I used to be Jose Mariposa back then and was (and still am) a huge Changeling The Dreaming Fan. I'm 36 now and I have been playing White Wolf games since I was a teenager at the tender age of 13.<br /> <br /> Oh I am also a Latino, Queer, Radical Leftistst, who loves anime, gothic horror, SCA, and handsome men. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","user":"Keichiokami","date":".  Had some important life changes, including change in employment. 04-27-2017, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:50:36-07:00","id":899352,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Xerxes, which has been my long-time handle since Librarium Online and Shadownessence in the early 2000s. I also go by Aramithius (a name unique to me in all the Interwubs, I think, but only used on Reddit and the Bethesda Forums) and CrucibleofWords.<br /> <br /> I'm from many places in the UK, currently in Basingstoke and desperately looking for people to run Exalted with. This may be solved soon, but any other on-location people would be appreciated. I have tried running things over Skype with people I have known for years, and it didn't really work, so I'm not overly confident in doing it with strangers. And between doing church activities at least 3 times a week, STing a once-a-month Dark Ages: Vampire game, and playing in a Vampire: the Masquerade Camarilla game, a Blood Bowl league and starting in a Necromunda campaign I generally want to either vegetate or sleep when I'm at home.<br /> <br /> I got into roleplaying games through the Fighting Fantasy gamebook series in the early 90s, was lent a copy of Tunnels &amp; Trolls and then made my own homebrew system that was a mash-up of the two. I got introduced to VtM in Sixth Form, but didn't actually get round to playing any until university, which also held such wonders as Star Wars d20, and such horrors as D&amp;D 3.5. I had a friend who ranted at length about the fantasticness of Exalted 2E (particularly the tick-based combat and the notion of an actual social combat system), but never played any. Fell in love with the feel of the game when I got the 2E PDF when it was given away for free, but never really looked at the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Then I saw Ex3 was out, got incredibly excited and jumped over from the Vampire OP forums to here. My life is currently my work and my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/870410-a-not-quite-newb-s-read-through-of-ex3?_=1464162181823&amp;_=1464205089436\">not-quite-newb readthrough of the Ex3 rulebook</a>. Oh wow, I've been at it a month. That is... scary. I look forward to posting more frequently when I won't encounter spoilerific things in the threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:57:18-07:00","id":899361,"title":"","content":"I'm Kukla. I live in Massachusetts in the USA. I got in to Exalted back in 2005-ish but virtually all of my games have been on the internet. I'm an upper class white male non-heterosexual STEM nerd, and I love to complain. The main reason I'm here is because I love to be salty and grumpy, and because I enjoy bickering as constructively as possible. I was briefly in charge of an Exalted MUSH, which went okay. I've written some for Sanguine Productions, and I'm very proud of my contributions to the Myriad Song game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":587,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","user":"Kukla","date":". 05-25-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:02:40-07:00","id":899368,"title":"","content":"Great idea for the thread! Thanks Totentanz.<br /> <br /> My name is Cameron, I've been an English/Drama teacher for most of my working life, though I'm currently the Communications Officer for the teachers' union in my state (NSW, Australia).<br /> <br /> I started playing WW games in the early 90s and still have my limited edition version of Exalted 1st ed sitting alongside similarly faux-leather bound versions of Mage and werewolf. Of all WW games the ones I've played the most are Exalted, Aberrant and Mage:the sorcerers crusade (back in the days of geocities I even used to maintain a site devoted to M:tSC) - I'm also heavily narrativist in my gaming, though as a long time Shadowrun player I'm not afraid to roll up my sleeves and get crunchy.<br /> <br /> I'm in the process of completing a masters degree in educational psychology in which I've been researching the use of role playing as a teaching tool, and I'm actually looking forward to getting back into the classroom to get back to lessons where students get to be heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:07:57-07:00","id":899376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899352#post899352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... currently in Basingstoke ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow, that's an actual place! I thought when Arthur Dent talked about the &quot;Basingstoke roundabout&quot; in Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, he was making up a space-y sounding name. (It doesn't seem space-y when you see it spelled out, but it didn't sound out of place in the radio show.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Angel Toaster from Keychain of Creation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7935-cartographer7","name":"Cartographer7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7935_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:16:46-07:00","id":899390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cartographer7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899376#post899376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow, that's an actual place! I thought when Arthur Dent talked about the &quot;Basingstoke roundabout&quot; in Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, he was making up a space-y sounding name. (It doesn't seem space-y when you see it spelled out, but it didn't sound out of place in the radio show.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The roundabout thing is also a joke. The question is which roundabout... we have many, many roundabouts. Probably at least one every half-mile or so. Not counting the mini-roundabouts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:27:22-07:00","id":899399,"title":"","content":"I've been playing WW games since 98 (&quot;Nineteen-Ninety-Eight?&quot; &quot;I know, hard to believe it was last millennium&quot;) and RPGs in general a little longer than that. I recently started a weekly 3E Dragon-Blooded game <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report\">Dynasty of Dovak</a>.<br /> <br /> Exalted is one of my favourite games: been into it since 1st Edition, but I don't get to play much (would be interested in joining an online game). Infernals are my favourite splat, followed by Dragon-Blooded then Alchemicals. Ledaal Kes is my favourite canon character. Keychain of Creation was my favourite webcomic.<br /> <br /> I'm was initially sceptical about 3E, but it's really grown on me as I've played it more. If you're on the fence, I'd urge you to look at it with fresh eyes and take the game &quot;as it is&quot; instead of what you think it <i>should</i> be. 3E is a great game, but it's very different to 2E -- if you approach it thinking it should be the same as 2E, you are going to be disappointed.<br /> <br /> I'm not afraid to post my opinions; but check my sig, they're just opinions. I'd love to hear your opinions, especially if you disagree with me. Hearing other points of view helps me build informed opinions and gain a better appreciation for Exalted. <br /> <br /> I am dyslexic and literally minded. I can have trouble conveying tone, but I try to be civil and am always happy to clarify myself. <br /> <br /> I hope you get a lot of use out of this forum<br /> <br /> Feel free to quote my posts when ever, where ever. Open to private messages.<br /> <br /> I don't answer questions about my personal life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-30-2020, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:44:05-07:00","id":899415,"title":"","content":"Eh, let's get in on this action.<br /> <br /> I'm SamuraiMujuru, the online handle I have used pretty much always. Inspired by my favorite character from Ninja Scroll, but dating back to a time of the internet where fact-checking was much less of a thing, so the sites had it misspelled. I do hosting support in Iowa.<br /> I've been playing Exalted since roughly a month after 1E came out, and it fast became the staple of my gaming group. We'd run the gamut from serious campaign to absolutely gonzo shenanigans. By the time second edition came out, I was stuck in the forever ST cycle. Every now and then, someone starts up a game, but every single time one or more of the players table flips and kills the game, leaving me incapable of actually PLAYING my favorite RPG.<br /> Been playing RPGs since 1991 with the big black box with the red dragon on the cover for D&amp;D, and my second RPG was RuneQuest. Since then I've branched into a little bit of everything, even going so far as to playing a World of Synnibarr one shot, just to see how bad it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:44:28-07:00","id":899417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cartographer7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899376#post899376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow, that's an actual place! I thought when Arthur Dent talked about the &quot;Basingstoke roundabout&quot; in Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, he was making up a space-y sounding name. (It doesn't seem space-y when you see it spelled out, but it didn't sound out of place in the radio show.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same reaction in school when one of my teachers offhandedly mentioned Basingstoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:56:40-07:00","id":899431,"title":"","content":"I'm Zee, and I'm a 27 year old first-generation immigrant living in beautiful Austin, Texas. I'm the co-founder of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_(discrete_mathematics)\" target=\"_blank\">graph</a> database/analytics startup, where we're in the process of signing our first enterprise customer!(!!!) I spend virtually all of my time working, and my posting here is accordingly real limited. Exalted 3e is my favorite pen and paper game ever, and Solars and Sidereals are tied for my favorite Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:57:19-07:00","id":899493,"title":"","content":"Well this looks fun!<br /> Secrets are more fun though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 02-25-2019, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:23:46-07:00","id":899516,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Ferryman. I am an unrepentent nerd who lives in San Diego county. I have worked in education for essentially all of my adult life, and have been reading/playing/running tabletop rpgs on and off for the last twenty years. I discovered Exalted right after 1st Edition was released by browsing the new arrivals shelf at the FLGS, spent the better part of an hour reading it in the aisle before I realized that I should really just buy the damned thing. Then I went straight home, devoured the rest of the hardback, and pitched it to my college friends. I still love the game, despite how hard it is these days to carve out time for it between my group's work schedules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899347#post899347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Keichiokami and I live in sunny San Diego. I work at an awesome gaming themed bar/grill called Tabletop Commons</div> </div> </div> </div>I have friends who have been there, but I haven't been myself! I guess I need to make the trip down from North County one of these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:33:34-07:00","id":899526,"title":"","content":"Oh boy.<br /> <br /> Well, I'm the pilot of the <s>Gundam</s> Warstrider Heavy Arms. I live in the strange Commonwealth of Pennsylvania (so Onyx Path HQ is supposedly somewhere nearby).<br /> <br /> I've been gaming most of my life, though I got started with war games with my dad before I discovered RPGs proper in '95 with WEG Star Wars. Soon after one of my WEG SW pals wanted to try out this weird new Vampire the Dark Ages thing in the summer of '96. I then got hooked on Werewolf the Apocalypse, Mage then Ascension, and WW's general catalog since. After missing the boat with my original group for Aeon, I got really excited when Exalted 1e came out and my new college gaming crew were on board; been a fan ever since.<br /> <br /> General other stuff about me: I'm a biologist, and Jewish (both of which come up more often than you might expect..) as far as what I tend to disclose online.<br /> <br /> I'm not a very frequent poster on Exalted stuff (though I lurk a lot), so I guess this sort of thread is also aimed at bringing folks like me back into things rather than just new posters. I burned out pretty hard during the 2e flames of yore, so I'm still testing the waters with 3e discussions; though I'm still a bit quiet since I haven't gotten to play 3e yet so I'm still in &quot;theory&quot; space with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:48:04-07:00","id":899542,"title":"","content":"I am Monkipi and like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1998_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1998\" data-vbnamecard=\"1998\">Keichiokami</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1315_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1315\" data-vbnamecard=\"1315\">Ferryman</a> I live in San Diego. I'm a student, a researcher, and someone who does general miscellany for a charter school development company. I also perform regularly at San Diego's National comedy theatre, where I met the majority of the cast for my actual play podcast.<br /> <br /> Been playing games since I was about 9 years old, with the WotC Star Wars RPG, so yeah, I'm young. I got the Exalted 2e core and Chageling: The Lost right before I entered high school and fell in love. I lost the books not 4 months later in one of San Diego's many wildfires. After getting the books back a few years later, I lurked around the forums throughout my late teens and never really left. <br /> <br /> I'm not a wildly prolific poster, unless I have made some art or am releasing an episode. I've tried to be more active in the discourse since 3e has come out. Some weeks are better than others. My favorite Exalts are Sidereals, and were I chosen I reckon I'd be a Chosen of Serenity or an Eclipse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:56:54-07:00","id":899551,"title":"","content":"Hi all! I'm Irked, which is... actually not that accurate of a personality description in general, I hope. I'm a college professor at a school near Pittsburgh; I got into roleplaying via the old Star Wars WEG system, discovered Mage: the Ascension in college, and picked up Exalted 1e not long after. I've been a forumgoer here for about the past decade; I played and read Second Ed pretty obsessively, though I've scaled back during the 2e/3e hiatus.<br /> <br /> I run a weekly 3e game for a few of my students, who have juuuuust hit Essence 3, and I've been part of a long-running rotating-GM game that recently converted over from Second Ed. I like mathematics and mechanics, so I'm mostly here for systems discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 05-25-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:36:12-07:00","id":899578,"title":"","content":"I'm Drew; over other forums and places I've gone mostly by Darius Solluman.<br /> <br /> I distinctly remember reading some of Grabowski's early Q&amp;As about Exalted and thinking it sounded like stupid powerwank fantasy. It didn't help that I was a mage fanboy and he went out of his way to knock the kind of freeform magick with a k that I thought was the coolest thing since sliced bread.<br /> <br /> I didn't re-evaluate until... oh, 2002. After I'd been exposed to Nobilis, I realized that power doesn't correlate to quality. I got into the old Exalted wiki pretty fierce, and ran a couple of games. And played in the Exalted Mush under Kukla, cause he's awesome.<br /> <br /> Since then... I've basically been stuck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:44:05-07:00","id":899582,"title":"","content":"Hey, folks. I'm Valles in all but one forum I ever posted in. I'm an early-thirties grocery store 'Courtesy Clerk' (I put things in bags) from Elkins, West Virginia. My first RPG experience was also the old WEG Star Wars, at summer camp in the... mid-early nineties? I discovered Exalted via the fanfic section of The Freedom Stone forums, at just about the right time to pick up MoEP: Alchemicals as my first purchase from the line.<br /> <br /> I play in a long-running play-by-post game that uses the FATE engine and an IRC chat game, and just last week started my own very first chat game. I will probably flail. (Not fail. Flail.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:47:03-07:00","id":899584,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, my first intro into Exalted...<br /> <br /> There was a webcomic (no longer updating now, sadly) called Keychain of Creation that really got me into the setting. I'm sure I'm one of many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:26:12-07:00","id":899622,"title":"","content":"That was a very good comic. So sad it stopped.<br /> <br /> I'm Ozzy, an English teacher at North-East Forestry University, Harbin, China. I'm actually British though.<br /> <br /> I played DnD as a teenager, and was in a really big Roleplaying society in university, where WW games were popular, so that's how I got into Exalted, by way of Old World of Darkness. I played a lot of Dragonblood games, Vampire, Mage, Qin, Dark Heresy, etc.<br /> Somehow, without meaning to, I seem to have only ended up playing Celestial Exalted. I'd like to play some other games, but I do like Exalted, so it's not so bad.<br /> I got fed up with it and stopped running it late in 2nd ed, but 3rd ed has reinvigorated my interest.<br /> I run a (now Essence 5) 3rd ed game, and play a low-powered 800xp 2nd ed game.<br /> Being as I'm in China, I play over Skype.<br /> <br /> I post here because while I enjoy talking to my students, I do like to see some actual non-basic English spoken/written. And it's good when I'm procrastinating.<br /> <br /> Also... one of the reasons I loved Exalted was for the east Asian and Anime influences. Now I live in China these interest me not at all, I'm much more interested in the pulp influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:41:03-07:00","id":899633,"title":"","content":"Hi all, I'm Aaron, and no, I don't expect you to share your given name just because I (and Colin) have done so. I won't be offended if you don't remember it, either.<br /> <br /> I go by Drake here, but some of you might be more familiar with the name Drake Noble (and corresponding Dracula avatar), or may even known me from other parts of the internet as AaronOfBarbaria.<br /> <br /> I've lived a bunch of places in the U.S.A. over the years, but Idaho has been home since I settled in after a lady named Katrina suggested I move out of the New Orleans area about 11 years ago.<br /> <br /> I don't work anymore (I had some serious health issues that got in the way, but I've since gotten them in control - now I am just reveling in not currently needing to work to live comfortably); but I used to be a cook, and I've done loads of customer service - I just keep the house in order and keep a steady flow of games going for my wife (who I'll probably never actually get married to for financial reasons) and our friends.<br /> <br /> Also, as if it wasn't already obvious, I'm prone to extreme openness - do please let me known if that ever makes any of you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in a wide array of games, and it was almost completely accidental that I ever got into Exalted - I was picking up some other book at a shop and saw a 1st edition Exalted book sitting on the shelf, and while I was intrigued by it at the time but couldn't get my D&amp;D group interested in trying a different shade of fantasy or my World of Darkness group interested in trying out a different flavor of White Wolf. So I didn't even buy the book, and barely even thought about the game at all for years. Then, once I had found myself in Idaho and found a FLGS to get in with a new group of players at, they were sitting down one day to play 2nd edition Exalted - I sat in on a session to see how the game looked in play, went home after and bought the PDF, stayed up the whole night studying it and building my first character, and then met up with the ST at the FLGS the next day after work to show him the character and ask if I could get in on the game.<br /> <br /> I was hooked so bad that it didn't even stop me when the rules system kept crushing my mind every time I tried to ST my own chronicle, and now with EX3 out Exalted has become my go-to game out of the whole collection of White Wolf/Onyx Path work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:22:46-07:00","id":899654,"title":"","content":"I am Spartacus. Just kidding. My handle is my real name. I live in Minneapolis, Minnesota and am active in the local geek/con community.<br /> <br /> I've been tabletop gaming for something like 30 years, and I'm not even all that old, really. I picked up 1E Exalted not too terribly long after it came out and even wrote a little 70-something page fan supplement about mortal heroes that is...a little embarrassing, now. Somewhere along the line I became a freelance writer for 1st Ed. Mage: The Awakening and have since gone on to write for other Onyx Path lines, including becoming one of the most prolific writers for Demon: The Descent.<br /> <br /> I kind of mostly skipped Exalted 2E, partially because it didn't sing to me quite as well at the time, but mostly because I didn't have a gaming group interested in playing it. I was absolutely thrilled with what I heard through the grapevine about 3rd Edition (just barely missed the KS, alas) and snapped it up as soon as I could. I'm looking forward to running it with sort of an alarming amount of eagerness. Epic fantasy was my first love, and the new edition meshes nicely with my game design sensibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:05:43-07:00","id":899682,"title":"","content":"Hi there I'm wiwuno. I'm a DG sales lead in South Carolina desperately struggling to introduce the hobby of table top gaming into a town that only knows how to speak football and beer. I've been playing table top for only about 4 years. I started running scion games but have touched on dnd and pathfinder before. I havent played or run exalted yet but hopefully sometime soon i will be able to really play this game. I discovered exalted on the TV Tropes site talking about it and my curiosity lead me to make this the very first table top game i ever allowed to consume my soul. i'm new to this forum. I've posted here and there and commented a bit but i doubt anyone will actually remember much of me yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:08:16-07:00","id":899684,"title":"","content":"Mockery here. Dallas-area office utility player (I get shoved from place to place to cover for various accounts and have a collection of security badges for hospitals, businesses, etc.). I'm 35 for now, and I've been interested in Exalted since it was first teased. So I've been around kind of since the beginning, and while this doesn't make me more right than anyone else, I sometimes forget that not everyone was here when Games of Divinity first came out.<br /> <br /> I've been really *playing* Exalted since shortly before 2e came out--because despite my interest in the game I really wouldn't grok it for years and didn't get a group until then--and I seem to end up behind the ST screen as often as not. I'm mostly a lurker, but every now and then--not in a while, now--I'll post a bit of homebrew.<br /> <br /> Also, if I end up getting your name for the White Elephant exchange, you're getting a Daiklave. Even if you ask for something else, a sword's gonna end up in there. It just keeps happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:27:41-07:00","id":899696,"title":"","content":"Kingcrackers. A Chinese Singaporean, a bisexual, and a Buddhist/Daoist/Confucian.<br /> <br /> From 2002 to 2012 I lived in Shanghai, where I got really interested in pen-and-paper RPGs, but due to where I lived, could not find anyone to play with, and instead read whatever books I could find, which included World of Darkness, Scion, and a handful of other games. As with many others, Keychain of Creation was what got me into Exalted. From 2012 to 2014 I served my mandatory military service, and following that, started pursuing higher education, where I also started to play pen-and-paper RPGs in earnest.<br /> <br /> I now play in a weekly Exalted campaign, with whatever few players I have been able to find: myself, one other player, and the ST. Better than nothing, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I also enjoy Apocalypse World, Fate Core, wuxia novels and TV shows, superhero comics, Journey to the West, Asian fantasy, and practicing my religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:40:13-07:00","id":899708,"title":"","content":"I am vampire hunter D. I have bennhere for almost 15 years, through 4 different forum format. I dont talk often, as I by the time I find a thread all these other people have it on page 5 already.<br /> <br /> I dont actually play, as I have no friends to play with. Hell, I have no friends. As a result, i have weak understandings of the crunch rules. But I love the setting and like making home brew.<br /> <br /> Oh, and be warned, I have a bad habit of drunk posting. Keep that in mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 05-26-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T21:05:53-07:00","id":899717,"title":"","content":"Well, you can see the name, clearly. <br /> <br /> I'm a bay-area based geek, working as a substitute (hopefully soon full time) teacher in the California East Bay. I've got a broad range of RPGs on my shelf ranging from various flavors of Dungeons &amp; Dragons, Pathfinder, a small dabbling of FATE, Palladium, and naturally an absolute ton of White Wolf. I've been big on Exalted since day one, going out of my way to get hold of the limited edition core book just because it was released a month earlier than the unlimited. I've been summoned by the release of Third Edition. I've got an old campaign I've been hoping to update to 3.0, but elements of it I know are going to have to wait until we've got functional rules for things like Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T21:22:54-07:00","id":899723,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Fata, and I'm pretty sick of my screen name!<br /> <br /> Software engineering student who plays with other software engineers; game designer and developer, social justice bard, been playing since the release of 1st edition. Also love Mage: The Awakening and Demon: The Descent. Came into exalted by way of The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I also have a habit of posting at 2am and drunk-posting........ which may or may not currently be the case &gt;.&gt; &lt;.&lt; &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Edit: I just noticed that this was my 1800th post. I'll celebrate by taking another drink!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m