:""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:36:55-07:00","id":899856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899805#post899805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite what my name, avatar, post's content and writing style suggests, I'm actually a guy. I also has ten degrees in Broken English and like to draw a lots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, new folks. If you see a Jen thread, check it out. You'll at the very least get some good art, and they almost always lead to really interesting discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T02:47:15-07:00","id":899885,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm a 30-something Aussie from the southern state of Victoria and currently reside in Melbourne.<br /> <br /> I've been running games since I was first introduced to roleplay in early high-school and have run a game of pretty much anything I could get my hands on, though I don't have the breadth of experience most other Storytellers of my time have since it's hard to get new content down here. <br /> <br /> By day I'm a boring-as-hell Mortgage Processor which is probably as exciting as it sounds but I solidly like my job and it gives me thinking time (well used to, iv'e been crazy busy for the last 18 months non-stop).<br /> <br /> By evening I'm a father of three young boys who take up an enormous amount of my free time (AND PATIENCE) and I mostly buck around on the forums while keeping one eye out on them so I start about a hundred more posts than I ever actually submit on any given day. I'm told I sound rude in text, which I try my best to avoid (and fail a lot apparently) so I suppose I should say, if you read something I've written and infer something insulting from it - most likely I haven't meant it.<br /> <br /> WHEN I HAVE THE TIME; I'm a highly narrative focused writer and storyteller though I love me some mechanical crunch to mess with as well in the case of games. I Absolutely love playing computer games even though I am completely rubbish at them, and honestly I think that makes it even more fun. My players tell me I'm one of the best GM's they've ever had which is nice, but I have trouble accepting it sometimes. I run two games currently and play in one and EX3 is probably one of the best games I have ever played. Period. I'm a super fan boy so I tend to avoid re-work threads and stating opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T05:37:45-07:00","id":899944,"title":"","content":"Hi, everyone.<br /> <br /> I'm LeTipex. I'm a frenchman who spent most of his life outside of France, even if I currently live and work in Paris. I'm nearly 30, and I work in nuclear energy (more specifically, making it safer.) I'm not going to bother with my real name, because it's pretty much unprononceable (why no, I'm not a Great Old One, what could possibly give you that idea?... Is it the orgy? It's the orgy, isn't it?)<br /> <br /> I started playing tabletop rpgs in my early teens, and I never stopped. I went throught a lot of games, and Exalted has been a bit of a passion for me since the last days of 1st ed. I'm fascinated by the game, especially since it's a big part of what requindled my interest for history, anthropology and sociology.<br /> <br /> I currently ST a campaign with friends called Chains of Silver and Blood (my third, after Dragons of Coral and The City of Salt), and I occasionnally dabble into mapmaking. I do maps for people on the forum when I have the time, collect images and music for my Exalted sessions (check my sig for all that!), and I (very) occasionnaly write stuff. I relish in bringing people to rpgs in general, and to Exalted in particular, but afaik I'm pretty much the only one of my aquaintances who frequents the forums.<br /> <br /> Outside of the game and work, I'm a martial arts enthusiast, an occasionnal environmental/social activist, an all-around geek, and a mean cocktail mixer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:58:24-07:00","id":900026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899856#post899856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously, new folks. If you see a Jen thread, check it out. You'll at the very least get some good art, and they almost always lead to really interesting discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely second this, even though most Jen posts make me feel like I expect people must feel when they are trying to read my hand-writing (which is like typical fast scribbled script that happens when using &quot;normal&quot; letters but also the 'only pick up the pen tip at the end of a word' rule of cursive - except as written by the writer's off-hand, because I'm not actually right-handed even though that's the only hand I can write with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:34:21-07:00","id":900062,"title":"","content":"I'm Ejtaka, another forum goer who is getting tired of his name, but refuses to change it. I've been Ejtaka for over twenty years in various online places, and momentum is a powerful thing.<br /> <br /> I am generally very tired when posting here because I usually only come here when I am going to work (payroll officer in Canada) or going home to my amazing wife. This is also why my typing often sucks. My phone is just a little bit too small.<br /> <br /> I game for two reasons: one os escapism, and the other is to solve systems. I started with AD&amp;D, moved on to Legend of the Five Rings, Shadowrun, and finally Exalted 1st. I own more games than I could ever play. <br /> <br /> I like Exalted because it exceeds the rather harsh limitations of many other games (back in AD&amp;D I remember being killed by a dog because I rolled only 1 hp for a starting character). The rules are also very well done compared to most other games I have played (yes, they are). Exalted 3 is especially good because there are so many ways to explore an individual character both mechanically and thematically. A single character concept can end up many different places.<br /> <br /> Also, Exalted is suitably epic for my esacapist fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:14:22-07:00","id":900159,"title":"","content":"I want to add something: I have been told my signature reads like it's supposed to be a joke, but actually it's 100% serious. I am very literal-minded. I really really don't know how to &quot;read between the lines&quot; and have trouble communicating without being misinterpreted. Also tend to misinterpret others' posts. I promise it's always acccidental and not me being a jerk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:45:08-07:00","id":900459,"title":"","content":"39Steps here, director of a performing troupe, and ancient player of tabletop RPGs. Cut my teeth on the first Monster Manual, and went on to lengthy forays into D&amp;D 1st and 3.5th eds., good old Champions, the entire original World of Darkness line, L5R, and finally, Exalted 2nd ed. My sessions GM'd to sessions played ratio is probably 50/1, even playing in my current (awesome!) Exalted Modern (2nd ed.) game via Skype. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are my true passion in Exalted, and to be honest, I'm just coming up to speed on Solars and the terrifying power of their Charmset. The best parts of 2nd ed. Exalted, IMHO, involved Yu Shan, Bureau politics, and having gods as neighbors. Also, Celestial Cocaine.<br /> <br /> My Forum contributions are few, but hopefully funny enough to warrant their existence. The Alpaca Out of Fucking Nowhere? That was me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:50:53-07:00","id":900464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=900459#post900459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Forum contributions are few, but hopefully funny enough to warrant their existence. The Alpaca Out of Fucking Nowhere? That was me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidently, the AlpacaOOFN created one of my favourite headcannons for Sidereals which i'm itching to get the chance to explore in 3rd Edition - thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:37:19-07:00","id":900534,"title":"","content":"I'm Philippe Saner, a statistician from Ottawa. If you care about my demographics, I'm a 21-year-old straight white male atheist.<br /> <br /> I like homebrew, mechanical analysis, and the occasional argument.<br /> <br /> 3e's my favourite edition but I'd be reluctant to play it out of the box. Other games I'm a fan of include DFRPG, Ars Magica 5, Sufficiently Advanced, and Burn Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:44:18-07:00","id":900540,"title":"","content":"Hi new people! I hope you guys like the forum!<br /> <br /> I'm Prometheus878, caucasian 28 year old male from Georgia, USA. Big fan of Exalted, even though I have yet to actually play it. Was a member on the old forum, been on this one since it's launch.<br /> <br /> I'm usually lurking, occasionally popping up to comment from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 05-26-2016, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:19:02-07:00","id":900560,"title":"","content":"I'm Mendez, but you can also call me Lula (my apelido da capoeira). I live in Harlem, New York.<br /> <br /> I describe myself as a full-time tabletop RPG writer, but really it's more like full-time-and-a-half. I write Scion and Geist for Onyx Path, 7th Sea for John Wick Presents, Fate and Bubblegumshoe for Evil Hat, Urban Shadows for Magpie, Ironclaw for Sanguine, Shinobigami for Kotodama Heavy Industries, lots and lots of things for Galileo Games \u2026 okay, this list is swiftly becoming impractical, but you get the picture, I could go on. I also GM professionally, mostly for kids, and then I <a href=\"http://dungeon-elementary.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">make fun of them on the Internet</a>. I have an undergraduate degree from Swarthmore College in Religion with minors in Dance and English Literature, as well as a master's degree from St. John's Graduate Institute in Eastern Classics; RPG writing is the first job I've ever had where I use both of my degrees all the time. My favorite role-playing games include Steal Away Jordan, Burning Wheel, anything Cortex Plus-based, and anything Apocalypse World-based.<br /> <br /> On the side, I also <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=157348&amp;ty=h\" target=\"_blank\">translate the Iliad from ancient Greek into hip hop</a>, for some reason.<br /> <br /> Outside of gaming, my interests include weird animals, diversity issues, and martial arts. If you meet me in real life and ask to spar me, I will pretty much always say yes, regardless of your style. If you go to conventions, I usually work Games on Demand at Gen Con. Come say hi and play something (and possibly fight me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:26:50-07:00","id":900568,"title":"","content":"Hello people!<br /> <br /> My name is Thiago Gueiros, and I'm a 33 years old, married, father of 2, SAP FI/CO consultant, born in and currently living in Recife, Northeastern Brazil, after having traveled and lived in many places in the Americas.<br /> <br /> I got into table top RPGs as a wee lad, 10 years of age through a game company called GROW's translation of D&amp;D that came in a boxed set with an adventure called &quot;Fuga da Masmorra de Zanzer Tem (Escape from Zanzer Tem's Dungeon)&quot;, in which I flipped out (and flipped the table) because I found the &quot;Iron Plate&quot; and ignored it because it was heavy and wtf do I wan't an iron plate for anyways? Then when another player (a female cousin of mine) came across it the DM saw it fit to explain it was actually the most powerful armor available. It didn't matter I was a Rogue with STR 6 (draconic 3d6, roll order character generation ftw, amirite?). That shit was mine and he just wanted to make out with her, the bastard.<br /> <br /> After fuming over it for a couple years, in 1995 (I'm now a man, 12 years old), First Quest Boxed Set was sold on brazillian newstands (which tend to be everywhere on the capitals). Me and a friend pooled our life savings together and purchased the set. It was pure glory since then. A couple more years in, as a misunderstood genius teen (aren't we all?), White Wolf came to crush the illusion of heroism. Fantasy was a farce. Personal horror was the true role playing experience. After a couple more years (and countless lives lived in Darkness), a wise and mature man of 16 became eccletic and was part of a vigorous scene, made up of a few dozen people. We played loads of AD&amp;D, D&amp;D3, WW, Toon, Paranoia, Shadowrun, Cyberpunk2020, Castle Falkenstein, BESM, GURPS and some brazillian systems, Arkanum(Trevas), Defesonres de T\u00f3quio (Tokyo Defenders) and probably a few others I can't remember right now.<br /> <br /> I always saw the Exalted books and thought they were cool, but I was already spending too much money on RPGs, and being a completionist (damn you D&amp;D3) made me not want to start collecting a new line. I was just learning what Kickstarter was when I stumbled upon Ex3's. I was flush with cash and decided I would finally start on this game that had caught my eye many years ago.<br /> <br /> And here we are now. I ST one game and play in 2, and am having a blast. I enjoy both fluff and mechanics discussions and writing very long and winded posts!<br /> <br /> Oh! And welcome to the forums!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-26-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:59:10-07:00","id":900601,"title":"","content":"Alright I guess.<br /> Hey I'm lionmanguy. Im nineteen right now, from Idaho, and I'll actually be graduating tomorrow. I've been reading rpg books since I was little but only got around to playing them on a regular basis recently. I have basically all the 2e books but have read very little of 1e.<br /> I actually made this account back when the very first leaks were posted on 4chan to try and let whoever know about it. Looking back it might have been a mistake the way i did it but hey, its over know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:04:09-07:00","id":900605,"title":"","content":"HI, everyone.<br /> <br /> I'm obviously not THE Ikari Gendo, I am over 50 years old, and work for a bank in the American Upper Midwest. I began table-top role playing in 1980 with 1st ed. D&amp;D. I've played everything from Champions to Traveller to the WEG D6 Star Wars (much better than either of the versions that followed). I have game mastered Savage Worlds, various editions of D&amp;D, Big Eyes Small Mouth, Teenagers From Outer Space, Exalted, and many other systems.<br /> <br /> I have a degree in English, but tend to post online when I should be sleeping, so I have problems with typos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:04:35-07:00","id":900649,"title":"","content":"Hi. I'm the UltraFennec. I'm [REDACTED] years old and I live in Kansas where the Koch brothers' robot mouthpiece holds sway and quashes all dissent while possibly committing voter fraud. I've been playing RPGs for nearly 17 years now, ever since I realized Baldur's Gate was actually a licensed game and picked up a 2e AD&amp;D starter game box. <br /> <br /> By day I mostly take care of invalid family members. By night I stalk the wilds keeping the spirits in balance and calling twisters on my enemies.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly here on the Exalted forum to chat with fellow people who play the game, despite my admittedly broad and large misgivings about the particular execution of the game, but I'm working on being less of a jerk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:01:05-07:00","id":900765,"title":"","content":"I'm a 30something from Melbourne (The real one, in Victoria, Australia, not that weird one in Florida, USA full of crazies); I've been gaming since I was about 5 (off and on with tabletop, pretty much non-stop as #pcmasterrace) First got into WW games with Werewolf 2nd, spent most of the 90's mainly playing WEG Star Wars (among others). In my spare time I study HEMA (mainly the Lichtenauer tradition), try to keep my puppa-dog entertained and sometimes play games.<br /> <br /> Like many others here, by the time I get around to an interesting topic it's 15 pages in and the posts I really want to respond to are on the first or second page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:16:51-07:00","id":900771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightwinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=900765#post900765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a 30something from Melbourne (The real one, in Victoria, Australia, not that weird one in Florida, USA full of crazies); I've been gaming since I was about 5 (off and on with tabletop, pretty much non-stop as #pcmasterrace) First got into WW games with Werewolf 2nd, spent most of the 90's mainly playing WEG Star Wars (among others). In my spare time I study HEMA (mainly the Lichtenauer tradition), try to keep my puppa-dog entertained and sometimes play games.<br /> <br /> Like many others here, by the time I get around to an interesting topic it's 15 pages in and the posts I really want to respond to are on the first or second page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another Aussie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:18:05-07:00","id":900772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899885#post899885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm a 30-something Aussie from the southern state of Victoria and currently reside in Melbourne.<br /> <br /> I've been running games since I was first introduced to roleplay in early high-school and have run a game of pretty much anything I could get my hands on, though I don't have the breadth of experience most other Storytellers of my time have since it's hard to get new content down here. <br /> <br /> By day I'm a boring-as-hell Mortgage Processor which is probably as exciting as it sounds but I solidly like my job and it gives me thinking time (well used to, iv'e been crazy busy for the last 18 months non-stop).<br /> <br /> By evening I'm a father of three young boys who take up an enormous amount of my free time (AND PATIENCE) and I mostly buck around on the forums while keeping one eye out on them so I start about a hundred more posts than I ever actually submit on any given day. I'm told I sound rude in text, which I try my best to avoid (and fail a lot apparently) so I suppose I should say, if you read something I've written and infer something insulting from it - most likely I haven't meant it.<br /> <br /> WHEN I HAVE THE TIME; I'm a highly narrative focused writer and storyteller though I love me some mechanical crunch to mess with as well in the case of games. I Absolutely love playing computer games even though I am completely rubbish at them, and honestly I think that makes it even more fun. My players tell me I'm one of the best GM's they've ever had which is nice, but I have trouble accepting it sometimes. I run two games currently and play in one and EX3 is probably one of the best games I have ever played. Period. I'm a super fan boy so I tend to avoid re-work threads and stating opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet another Aussie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:21:40-07:00","id":900773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=900459#post900459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">39Steps here, director of a performing troupe, and ancient player of tabletop RPGs. Cut my teeth on the first Monster Manual, and went on to lengthy forays into D&amp;D 1st and 3.5th eds., good old Champions, the entire original World of Darkness line, L5R, and finally, Exalted 2nd ed. My sessions GM'd to sessions played ratio is probably 50/1, even playing in my current (awesome!) Exalted Modern (2nd ed.) game via Skype. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are my true passion in Exalted, and to be honest, I'm just coming up to speed on Solars and the terrifying power of their Charmset. The best parts of 2nd ed. Exalted, IMHO, involved Yu Shan, Bureau politics, and having gods as neighbors. Also, Celestial Cocaine.<br /> <br /> My Forum contributions are few, but hopefully funny enough to warrant their existence. The Alpaca Out of Fucking Nowhere? That was me.</div> </div> </div> </div>39Steps is one of my all-time favourite plays. I shall try not to project expectations on to you ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T01:34:33-07:00","id":900777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightwinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=900765#post900765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a 30something from Melbourne (The real one, in Victoria, Australia, not that weird one in Florida, USA full of crazies); I've been gaming since I was about 5 (off and on with tabletop, pretty much non-stop as #pcmasterrace) First got into WW games with Werewolf 2nd, spent most of the 90's mainly playing WEG Star Wars (among others). In my spare time I study HEMA (mainly the Lichtenauer tradition), try to keep my puppa-dog entertained and sometimes play games.<br /> <br /> Like many others here, by the time I get around to an interesting topic it's 15 pages in and the posts I really want to respond to are on the first or second page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ayeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee... Hows this cold snap treating you? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T03:27:11-07:00","id":900808,"title":"","content":"I'm learning more about you guys from this thread than from 15 years perusing the forum.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:08:41-07:00","id":900868,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">GROWLS</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>The Frustrated Penwright of Mercurial Mindset</b><br /> <i>also known as &quot;Growls-at-the-Moon&quot; (Shadownessence), Dalerik (RPG.net / FreedomStone) and kungfufenris (Twitch)</i><br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> Hello.<br /> As you may have noticed from the blurb, I'm Growls. A 20-something Dane from the city of Aarhus.<br /> <br /> I'm currently stuck in a dead-end job, trying to figure out a way to get paid for something I'm actually good at.<br /> So. While I'm figuring that out, I'm engaging myself in roleplaying.<br /> To me, it's how I keep myself socially engaged as a communal activity with my friends and a way to make some interesting stories to keep my mind engage.<br /> <br /> I've been role-playing since 1999, first as a LARP, since as a P&amp;P'er, and the hobby has pretty much turned into a way of life for me.<br /> My first experience with Exalted was at a convention in 2003, where a vendor had the Limited Edition Corebook for sale. I found a few of the books and began reading blurbs. I did not catch 99% of the nuances but 15 year old Growls was intrigued. Until that point, D&amp;D had been the most advanced Fantasy experience for me.<br /> I borrowed a pile of books from a friend after thoroughly reading &quot;Aspect Book: Earth&quot; and being enthralled by the world within. And I never looked back.<br /> <br /> Somehow, Exalted's editions being a crazy relationship really fits my experience. I once saw a parable about that, yet I had to write my own.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>A head over heels in teenage-romance with 1st Edition, the cute hippy from the OWoD family, but the family's demands kept pulling our dreams into a system where they did not really fit, and the we ended up smoking and boozing as a way to deal with our issues, ignoring the problems, in the end not really knowing why we drifted apart. We had a lot of oneshots. A single campaign, and we had no real idea of what we ever doing, even though the ideas of an epic Dragonblooded campaign was talked about a lot in the late summer nights.<br /> <br /> Then, a year after high school Exalted came back as 2nd Edition, having got her act together, all sleek and codified in it's mind, trying to be the coolest thing on the block.<br /> Yet, slowly I realized just how broken Exalted really was, (mostly because the times she burned my gaming group with the rules) and those designer drugs were not helping.<br /> Three campaigns came and went, none of them really clicked the way it had back when we were dumb kids.<br /> <br /> And even through we tried, it fell apart, with Exalted checking into Rehab while I took to travelling around the world.<br /> <br /> Exalted came out of rehab in 2012 with 2.5. We tried again and it was better. But not really what I was looking for in a gamesystem at the time. I was seeing other games.<br /> I even tried conversions a few times, but it never really felt like Exalted, and really hollow.<br /> I sold off my books, and was pretty that would be it for Exalted and me.<br /> <br /> Then the Kickstarter appeared.<br /> And from what I was hearing, it sounded like Exalted had found that spark again. The one we bonded over back in our teens.<br /> I waited a long time for news, even made some plans in my head for campaigns from the snippets that drifted across the internet. Imagining great and amazing things.<br /> And when Exalted returned on release day, I doubled down in a flash of commitment. This was the game I was looking for all these years. </i></span> </div> </div> </div>Currently, I'm running a campaign, with another on the drawing board. And even though there is still a lot of demanding issues in the game, it fits my temperament perfectly.<br /> <br /> Of course, my schedule is also filled with other games, so I run and play a lot of different things. Blades in the Dark, L5R, D&amp;D5E, SW: EOTE, WFRP2, Malifaux.<br /> But Exalted means a lot to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:21:05-07:00","id":900876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=900808#post900808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm learning more about you guys from this thread than from 15 years perusing the forum.....</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i849.photobucket.com/albums/ab56/texisman/The-Simpsons-Mr-Burns-Excellent.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:57:41-07:00","id":901225,"title":"","content":"I guess I somehow became something of a semi-active poster recently, might as well introduce myself.<br /> <br /> Hello, I'm Ahmed, Also known as Chaoticag online, and cag and/or bean by friends. I'll just say I live in the middle east. But I had lived a decent chunk of my life in the states due to reasons.<br /> <br /> I tried running 2nd ed way back when a friend of mine got me interested in it, that went badly, but I still maintained interest in the setting and stuff. Still half-regret not backing 3rd edition exalted, since it fixes most my main concerns with 2nd ed. Looking to run a game of it currently, but waiting for a friend of mine to recover from something before I get us started. Still hoping I one day get in a game, but such is the fate of the dedicated game master. Still having fun running things at least.<br /> <br /> Other hobbies include videogames, reading, and seeing how long I can go on before people catch on that I'm not an American. Especially during conversation, heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11515-chaoticag","name":"Chaoticag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:16:37-07:00","id":901307,"title":"","content":"Hi! I am Daniel. I am a Brazilian translator, using my knack for languages (see: what I am posting right now, for instance!) to earn a living. I live in Rio de Janeiro, and have been an Exalted fan since... hell, 2004, when I was introduced to it by my now-ex girlfriend. I used to post things in the old Wiki by the name GoldenCat, since for a little while, I was trying to get away from the name 'Colapso', which I had created for a Superhero character (who was... basically a Sidereal, see the stars-in-the-face on my avatar), and I was trying to get away from my superhero past. No such luck, it turns out your first nickname follows you, and I have since relaxed about it (and even played my namesake in games since.) The name came from a GURPS Supers character, and while I love that system, I really can't go back to it anymore. Had fun playing FATE, DnD, and some less well-known systems like Cthulhutech and others since, however.<br /> <br /> I ran a very, very long mixed game, and a couple smaller ones since. I love to homebrew things, as my full page in the old wiki would show, as well as the many, many things not in it. I pretty much didn't make the jump to 2e, as the tone of the corebook just turned me off... and it was only a few things I heard about 3e that made me pay attention to Exalted again, despite running and playing 1e pretty extensively during 3e's lifetime. I got my hands on the 3e leak, and... hell, despite all that we had written for 1e (we called it 1.5, even), I made the jump, as it really, really won me over in several levels.<br /> <br /> And other than Exalted and other games... I suppose I like fantasy and pulp novels, historical and sociological writings, comic books and superheroes and manga in general, and... things.<br /> <br /> Currently running Daybreak, the insane 17-player-and-rising 3e game. It's tough, but quite a bit of fun. And explosions. But explosions are often fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 05-27-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:03:42-07:00","id":901362,"title":"","content":"I'm that guy what is who is being Beans.<br /> <br /> I tried playing Pathfinder about five? Five years ago? I dunno, it didn't work. I read about WW stuff and thought Exalted sounded cool, and then one day I sort of ended up in a campaign. I picked a Sidereal as my first character and did not have the Anathema program, so I was baffled and dying at first. I liked it enough to want to play more, though, and... well, here I am, I guess. Of the few I've played, my favorite chronicle was us as an Abyssal circle looking for our Lunar mates. We called it Waifuquest, because.<br /> <br /> My favorite Exalt splat is probably Abyssals, then Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I'm a Classics major a few summer classes from graduating, hopefully getting a job as an SAT/ACT tutor, and going for a Master's in teaching Latin. I'm on GITP as Beans also, and probably on Twitter being a meme war criminal or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T19:10:51-07:00","id":901640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=901307#post901307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! I am Daniel. I am a Brazilian translator, using my knack for languages (see: what I am posting right now, for instance!) to earn a living. I live in Rio de Janeiro, and have been an Exalted fan since... hell, 2004, when I was introduced to it by my now-ex girlfriend. I used to post things in the old Wiki by the name GoldenCat, since for a little while, I was trying to get away from the name 'Colapso', which I had created for a Superhero character (who was... basically a Sidereal, see the stars-in-the-face on my avatar), and I was trying to get away from my superhero past. No such luck, it turns out your first nickname follows you, and I have since relaxed about it (and even played my namesake in games since.) The name came from a GURPS Supers character, and while I love that system, I really can't go back to it anymore. Had fun playing FATE, DnD, and some less well-known systems like Cthulhutech and others since, however.<br /> <br /> I ran a very, very long mixed game, and a couple smaller ones since. I love to homebrew things, as my full page in the old wiki would show, as well as the many, many things not in it. I pretty much didn't make the jump to 2e, as the tone of the corebook just turned me off... and it was only a few things I heard about 3e that made me pay attention to Exalted again, despite running and playing 1e pretty extensively during 3e's lifetime. I got my hands on the 3e leak, and... hell, despite all that we had written for 1e (we called it 1.5, even), I made the jump, as it really, really won me over in several levels.<br /> <br /> And other than Exalted and other games... I suppose I like fantasy and pulp novels, historical and sociological writings, comic books and superheroes and manga in general, and... things.<br /> <br /> Currently running Daybreak, the insane 17-player-and-rising 3e game. It's tough, but quite a bit of fun. And explosions. But explosions are often fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please start a thread outlining how you go about managing such a large game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T01:32:39-07:00","id":901874,"title":"","content":"Hi all! I'm not one to share my name online, but most folks call me Garg anyway, so... there you go.<br /> <br /> I am *ahem* rapidly approaching my fourth decade. I've been gaming for rough 3/4s of that time. As you might guess, I've tried a lot of games over the years. Current favorites include Dungeon World &amp; Masks (Both Powered by the Apocalypse games), Ex3, FFG's Star Wars line, and Champions (HERO). Currently running a Force &amp; Destiny campaign and getting my Ex3 game off the ground after wrapping up a Dungeon World campaign. I'm also a big video gamer, which I'm sure is terribly shocking. IRL, I work in e-commerce.<br /> <br /> Unlike most old-timers, I did not start with D&amp;D. I could give the &quot;resume&quot;, but let's just say it's long and move on. I've been doing this long enough that I get excited about theory, gaming models, design, etc. I remember the first stirrings of White Wolf in my area (Silicon Valley) were Vampire LARPs - which I felt I was way too uncool to indulge in at the time, probably to my detriment.<br /> Exalted-wise, I bought the first edition on a whim, but I never really got a chance to do a serious game of it until Ex3. We've only just started. I'm liking how the system(s) hang together so far. Really aching for Arms of the Chosen, but I do enjoy homebrewing.<br /> <br /> Editorially, I think this thread is a smart move for the community in terms of being more welcoming so I wanted to support it. Someone in one thread or another mentioned that a glossary would be helpful - I totally second that idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11647-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T04:37:08-07:00","id":901952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gargoyle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=901874#post901874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Editorially, I think this thread is a smart move for the community in terms of being more welcoming so I wanted to support it. Someone in one thread or another mentioned that a glossary would be helpful - I totally second that idea!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/900499-exalted-forum-guide-to-helpful-topics-and-tags\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/900499-exalted-forum-guide-to-helpful-topics-and-tags\"> Exalted Forum Guide to Helpful Topics and Tags - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/900499-exalted-forum-guide-to-helpful-topics-and-tags\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/900499-exalted-forum-guide-to-helpful-topics-and-tags </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Helpful Topics The Official Exalted Forum Introduction Thread (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We are compling a glossary there. If there are any terms you aren't familiar, post in that thread and let us know! <br /> <br /> Welcome to the forum! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T04:48:09-07:00","id":901955,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> Thought I should post an introduction here as well.<br /> <br /> I got introduced to roleplaying in my early teens. A friend at school mention he had been trying a cool kind of game, talked about it. I actually don't know if it was Dungeons and Dragons, Drakar och Demoner (a Swedish RuneQuest derivate), or something else. It was a sanbboxy game, and it was without any mechanics and we just free-formed it (so now you know where my disrespect for RAW comes from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). I loved it, and later that year, around Christmas, I bough the Drakar and Demoner Box.<br /> <br /> While impovising a lot, and just seeing mechanics as support or things to disregard, I still have a fascination of them, and prefer the mechanics to be in sync with the game. So I can switch between using them and just freeform, without it being an obvious switch.<br /> <br /> During my teens, I GM'ed a lot and played some. I also spent quite a bit of my money back then on more roleplaying stuff. So I have quite a few different settings and systems lying around at home, not counting my own homebrews.<br /> <br /> Adult life have definitely made gaming being less common. Being really picky of how I want to roleplay, and apparently not being in the main stream, isn't helping either. I haven't tried much voice or video chat yet, but hopefully that suits me; and as it would really increase the area to find fellow gamers...<br /> <br /> I first heard about Exalted from a coworker, as I was talking about if a gaming idea I had for a &quot;god level&quot; game. I bought both first and second edition core rule PDFs, ST companions and a few other books. Then I bought both the PDF bundles for first and second edition, and a while later starting to get some hardcovers (well, some for first editon, and almost all for second edition). So yes, I have bought the Second Edition core book three times... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Came for the mechanics. Stayed for the setting. I don't really like the over the top kung-fu stuff, which seems to be a common appeal. But because I love exploring different cultures and mindset, while also being bored to death by the standard medieval Tolkienesque fantasy, Exalted hits almost all the notes for me.<br /> <br /> While second edition isn't a perfect fit for me, it is the one closest to what I want. Now that I have Ex3, I plan to mod 2ed with stuff from 1ed and Ex3. What I really would want to do is a complete overhaul, which I tend to refer to as &quot;Edition L&quot;. However, even if I ever get that down into a written format, comprehensible to others, that would be way off into the future.<br /> <br /> I have noticed that my comfort zone might be a bit wider than most, and even if I try to censor myself, I might voice opinions or ideas that squick others out. I guess hanging out in BDSM circles, being an agnostic (with a hard atheistic leaning), and being a Scandinavian leftish liberal might be part of it. Or I'm just a sick dude... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some other notes... Work with computers and been an IT-consultant for most of my career. Was in an urban warfare specialist battalion in the army. Did a lot of martial arts in my late teen (logged my hours one of the years and realized I did slightly above 500 hours that year) and kind of still having an itch to get back into doing it. Trying to learn dancing Salsa and Bachata, and finally feel I'm starting to grasp the basics.<br /> <br /> Oh... and I tend to do long-winded posts at times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T14:50:28-07:00","id":902295,"title":"","content":"I'm a biologist and illustrator from Mexico City. I began playing Exalted back in 2001, but my gaming group broke around 2011, so I haven't played Exalted as frequently as I used to. However, to feed my own Exalted hunger I started a webcomic in 2012. I sometimes take character commissions, or upload some random sketches to share with the community here. Drawing stuff makes me happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T08:44:10-07:00","id":904976,"title":"","content":"I realised that I should probably introduce myself since I've been wandering the forums, disagreeing with people and giving out opinions and likes. Unlike some forumites, I don't have any useful skills or talents to share with the community. I am not a professional anything, which is not to say that I have no job, merely that I have no profession. I'm in Exeter, but I am not English. I am overjoyed that I can A: Access this site from work and B: Log in to post during my dull days. I'm learning Polish, slowly, because Polish is stupid, and people who attempt to learn it as a second language are more stupid still. I am also done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:08:20-07:00","id":905837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=904976#post904976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm learning Polish, slowly, because Polish is stupid, and people who attempt to learn it as a second language are more stupid still. I am also done.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I know of the Polish language you'll need an excess amount of Cs and Zs, and try shoving gravel in your cheeks to imitate the accent.<br /> <br /> Source: My girlfriend (more accurately: Wife every way but legally) has Polish ancestry and studies other languages out of genuine interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T21:49:42-07:00","id":906202,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. My name is Michael, and I am a long time Exalted Player, having bought my first Exalted book in the Summer of 2001. I have been hooked on the style of gaming ever since.<br /> <br /> Wick Black is a character I created long ago. With Exalted 3rd Edition, I can make her a real Exalt. Though, not a Solar or a Lunar, as some thought she might turn out. Exalted of Plentimon sounds like a pretty cool thing.<br /> <br /> See you on the flip side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:07:11-07:00","id":906740,"title":"","content":"Heyo!<br /> <br /> I'm relatively new to Exalted. I got really into 2E but never actually got to play more than a few sessions, and now I'm super excited to take part in all the new stuff with 3E. The sheer depth and breadth of the lore has hooked me forever, and I love all the customization aspects, despite not being terribly sure about balance, which is why I started hanging around here. I've only played a Solar, but not for lack of desire--I definitely want to try a Sidereal the first chance I get, but in 2E no one in our party was interested in being a Solar, so I took it up.<br /> <br /> I'm a writer and editor by trade, currently living in southern US (pray for me) but will be moving westward by July on the first major step of my life post-school. When I get there, I plan to sucker in my friend's roommates into a game (and my first attempt STing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:18:33-07:00","id":907130,"title":"","content":"Hello. I'm Aranfan. I used to be on the old White Wolf Forums before they went poof.<br /> <br /> Getting back into exalted now that 3rd Edition is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:36:52-07:00","id":911822,"title":"","content":"I'm Gailedon I've been playing RPG's for over 30 years now, mostly various incarnations of D&amp;D but also White Wolf games. I started playing Exalted back around 2004, and have been a pretty big fan through it's various incarnations. I played on the old Exalted chats on the WW page. I'm currently a student finishing up my doctorate in chiropractics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11924-gailedon","name":"Gailedon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T18:35:58-07:00","id":912564,"title":"","content":"So, I just realized that though I've had an account here for over a year, I haven't posted anything. But hi, I'm VolatileSublime, also known in meatspace as Nina. <br /> <br /> I actually haven't been here in a whiiiiile, but 3E called me back. I do like that people seem to try to be more welcoming to newer members now, and I may attempt to be less self-conscious and delurk more often. <br /> <br /> I've been into Exalted since the 1E core first came out. In fact, that was one of the first purchases I paid for with money from my job. I haven't really played much, due to lack of opportunities close to where I live. Plus, every time I tried to join an online game, it seemed there were either scheduling or ego conflicts. <br /> <br /> I've managed to get a few people at work into 3E, so as soon as they finish their character sheets, I'll be running a chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm kinda ridic excited, tho they're already side-eying the pile of plot notes I've accumulated...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5574-volatilesublime","name":"VolatileSublime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5574_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:42:18-07:00","id":916006,"title":"","content":"Your avatar looks familiar, but I'm not sure. Is it Ameratsu from the Wicked + the Divine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T01:46:02-07:00","id":916078,"title":"","content":"Good eye! Yep, that's her. WicDiv's one of my favorite comivs coming out right now. When people mention that they want to get into comics but aren't sure where to start, that's usually the one I shove at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5574-volatilesublime","name":"VolatileSublime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5574_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:35:42-07:00","id":916235,"title":"","content":"Hey all, as can be told by my post-count, I lurk more than I post on this forum. I go by guildsbounty or GB, and that's the only name I've ever gone by on the net...so if you see a guildsbounty somewhere, it's probably me. I'm a software engineer, hobbyist mad scientist, leather-worker, martial artist, and general nerd with a penchant for long-winded explanations that usually (though not so much on this forum) tend to branch off into the sciences by way of explanation.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of details about far more game systems than I have had the opportunity to play, mostly due to time constraints and difficulty in finding people to play with...currently DMing a D&amp;D 5e game and putting together pieces for a Shadowrun 5E game that will, honestly, probably never actually get played.<br /> <br /> I tend to like a pretty even split between crunch and fluff, and have several in-progress stories using Exalted that will likely never get finished because I have trouble finding time to write, and often lose interest in a story before I have a chance to take it too far. The current one I'm mucking around with follows a Chosen of Secrets who is Chair (and only functional member) of the Convention on the Multiverse. I'm also something of a chronic worldbuilder, and generally enjoy designing worlds and settings more than telling stories in them (part of why I tend to wander off from stories after a while). It's why I like DM/GM/STing so much.<br /> <br /> In terms of Exalted, I've mucked around with 2 and 3E a bit, though nothing for very long...but am blessed (cursed?) with a bizarre memory that absorbs RPG rulebooks (and other technical things) like a sponge, even though I can't remember what I had for dinner three days ago, and often struggle to remember someone's name. So I do actually know quite a lot about how the game works. My favorite splats are Siddies and Solars, but I certainly have appreciation for all the other splats as well. My love for worldbuilding and (sometimes annoyingly) accurate memory for rulebooks does make me tend towards homebrewing as a solution to issues within a system, and I put together an Exalted Modern setting a while back...around the same time Shards came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T17:13:20-07:00","id":916499,"title":"","content":"Greetings, all! My name is Angela and I'm a long-time roleplayer. I was into Vampire the Masquerade, Shadowrun, and D&amp;D back in high school. Now, I'm a long since graduated from college 30-something who's finally re-discovering her love of tabletop gaming. My friend sucked me into his Exalted game last year where I play a no-nonsense Righteous Devil Eclipse Caste. It's been loads of fun and I'm happy to be gaming again!<br /> <br /> I'm a professional artist and writer by day and the author of the art howto book, <a href=\"http://www.angelicshades.com/angelic-visions-book/\" target=\"_blank\">Angelic Visions</a>. I have a passion for character and fantasy art and have been using Exalted as an excuse to expand my portfolio of art into more interesting avenues of design and high fantasy. I've already created Exalted-inspired art and fiction which you can see <a href=\"http://theuncrucified.angelasasser.com\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I also dabble in mask-making with leather and other crafty endeavors and love helping out other artists.<br /> <br /> Glad to be here among kindred spirits!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/918857-ang-s-exalted-sketchbook\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Art</a> | <a href=\"http://theuncrucified.angelasasser.com\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Fanfiction</a>","edited":{"userid":11990,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11990-angelicshadow","user":"angelicshadow","date":". 06-17-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11990-angelicshadow","name":"angelicshadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:55:35-07:00","id":916976,"title":"","content":"Hello everybody!<br /> On the old White Wolf forums, I was known as Ominous_Presence. I sorta fell of the face of the forums shortly after 2E released, but hearing about 3E brought me back ( I sadly missed hearing about it in time to back it). <br /> I've been playing rpg's since my single-digit years, mostly D&amp;D, various WW games, and some Shadowrun. <br /> I'm in my 30's and working towards completing my college education in ancient history and mythology, once I move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:05:34-07:00","id":917308,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm Demetrius7997, AKA Mr Demmywinks (Thanks JimB, the silly name stuck.) I've been a tabletop gamer since 2000, so 16 years... 16 years this month actually. I got suckered into storytelling within the first couple months of gaming and have been doing it regularly ever since. I've mostly played White-Wolf games, but in the lengthy Exalted absence I've branched out. I've been off and on the forum pretty much the whole time I've been gaming. A few years back I did a stint as a mod here. Off the forum I'm a stay at home dad. My son has been raised around the hobby and has recently joined in, and has shown an interest in storytelling as well. Oh, I met my wife through my original gaming group. I think that's enough about me for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:05:44-07:00","id":928321,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I'm PraxisCat. I'm a player / sometimes ST in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a>'s current game, and I'm fairly new to tabletop. (1 year of various games and systems + a number of oWoD hunter 1shots and a D&amp;D 3-shot). I really like the cinematic flair that Exalted's combat system allows for.<br /> <br /> I'm really interested in mechanics of tabletops and in homebrewing, and am interested overall in learning to make unobtrusive but rich and complex systems that work well. I'm know that's a skill that requires a lot of practice, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":". 07-11-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T11:42:54-07:00","id":930957,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Tikor and have used the name around various parts of the internet for a couple of decades. Tikor is not always me (it is short and sometimes taken), but I am always Tikor. The name is from my first playthrough of Ocarina of Time, I thought it sounded Kokiri in origin (and I knew Kokiri from Nintendo Power).<br /> <br /> My first Exalted book was a second-hand Wonders of the Lost Age I picked up at Half Price Books. I was in a 2e game at the time, and I had borrowed and read all of my ST's books and decided it was time for me to expand our combined collection. I have since picked up a good-sized bookshelf of Exalted that sits next to my home computer. I have a habit of reading a few pages from a randomly selected supplement while the machine boots up. This is related to me bringing canon into a number of threads. I used to contribute 2e homebrew to the wiki. I prototype boardgames for fun, so I connect to Exalted on a mechanical level. <br /> <br /> I am a 30 something professional, with 30 something professional friends, who are all enthusaistic over drinks about the ideas in Exalted as I explain them but do not prioritize getting together to play in any medium. They're mostly D&amp;D veterans. So I interact with Exalted through fanfiction, both reading and writing (since I've long since read and re-read the sourcebooks and the 6 book novel series). So I connect to Exalted on a narrative/fluff level.<br /> <br /> I am an atheist who would completely turn that lack of belief around in Creation. I'm open to changing my mind when hearing a good argument, which is what I visit these boards for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T07:20:15-07:00","id":931332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=930957#post930957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm Tikor and have used the name around various parts of the internet for a couple of decades. Tikor is not always me (it is short and sometimes taken), but I am always Tikor. The name is from my first playthrough of Ocarina of Time, I thought it sounded Kokiri in origin (and I knew Kokiri from Nintendo Power).<br /> <br /> My first Exalted book was a second-hand Wonders of the Lost Age I picked up at Half Price Books. I was in a 2e game at the time, and I had borrowed and read all of my ST's books and decided it was time for me to expand our combined collection. I have since picked up a good-sized bookshelf of Exalted that sits next to my home computer. I have a habit of reading a few pages from a randomly selected supplement while the machine boots up. This is related to me bringing canon into a number of threads. I used to contribute 2e homebrew to the wiki. I prototype boardgames for fun, so I connect to Exalted on a mechanical level.<br /> <br /> I am a 30 something professional, with 30 something professional friends, who are all enthusaistic over drinks about the ideas in Exalted as I explain them but do not prioritize getting together to play in any medium. They're mostly D&amp;D veterans. So I interact with Exalted through fanfiction, both reading and writing (since I've long since read and re-read the sourcebooks and the 6 book novel series). So I connect to Exalted on a narrative/fluff level.<br /> <br /> I am an atheist who would completely turn that lack of belief around in Creation. I'm open to changing my mind when hearing a good argument, which is what I visit these boards for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blessed Be Half Price, for it allows nerds to trade books without actually interacting with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T01:09:43-07:00","id":934344,"title":"","content":"I'm Sandact6, and I'm the most fucking awesome person you'll ever meet. From my crib on the Moon to the rockstar life I live, if I said anything more than that than your own head would explode from the sheer awesomeness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Currently living in Edmonton Alberta and aiming to go back to school while trying to find a job <i>any job</i> in the meantime. I got into Exalted shortly after 2e Sidereals was launched, and it wasn't until much later I tried making homebrew for after I devoured all the books and became a bit too familiar with the rules. I do writing time to time as an inspiring writer and have been doing so for nearly 17 years or so. I now do lots of homebrew which you find in the signature, and will probably do more as I continue to remain NEET until I find this mythical thing called employment or school starts again.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:18:23-07:00","id":935118,"title":"","content":"Hey people! I've been playing exalted since late first edition. I really liked the broken initiative system of first edition a lot *ducks*. I'm hailing from the great NW USA, been gaming since I was like 11 or 12 when I was still into AD&amp;D 2nd ed. I transitioned into white wolf games with first edition werewolf, then vampire, wraith and mage...I thought that was all pretty cool (i'm nerdy). I've been around on the WW forums, pre and post forum (multi) change, then through ccp , then onyx paths. I seam to have lost my logins or one of them got hacked or something. So I created a new one. So hello again! I've played in 1st and 2nd edition of Exalted, ran a couple 2nd ed games, wrote my own head cannon, compiled all of the solar charms from 2.5 and 2.0 into a crazy ass word file and totally nerded out on this game a lot. I'm currently in the process of getting some hard core shadow run nerds into exalted and man it's rough. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:49:55-07:00","id":939914,"title":"","content":"Uhm, hello.<br /> <br /> I'm TheFoolishBlackbird, a college student presently in South America. I've had an interest in Exalted for some years... I remember getting excited about the release of the third edition in high school. Recently, I bought the third edition, which I DM for my friends. I like indie rpgs, classic rpgs, card games, board games and reading.<br /> <br /> It's a pleasure to be part of this forum, and I hope I can start interesting friendships here!<br /> <br /> Uhm, they/them/their pronouns are preferred. Thank you kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12202-thefoolishblackbird","name":"TheFoolishBlackbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:11:56-07:00","id":940945,"title":"","content":"Hello~!<br /> <br /> I'm Sorcerous Overlord. It's been 6 months since I last tried to conquer a city-state.<br /> <br /> <i>Hi Sorcerous</i>.<br /> <br /> In actuality, I'm a English Teacher living in Japan. Exalted is my favorite rpg and favorite setting in general. I haven't had a chance to play 3rd yet, so I obsessively read and design characters to scratch that itch. If you want any character names or fluff written, please message me. I do that for a hobby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T17:31:18-07:00","id":941541,"title":"","content":"Oh...that's what this thread is. Welp, I'm Epee102. I read alot of second edition, never really was able to get a game off the ground. Really got into the lore right at the tail end of it, even tried to start an all Infernals game as my first exalted game (that went...poorly). Mythology, history, and anthro geek. Um. Yeah. Hi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T06:52:11-07:00","id":944817,"title":"","content":"Hello! I'm ... a privacy fanatic so I won't share personal details here. I hope that's ok.<br /> <br /> But I can share my Exalted experience! I've been a player of Exalted since early 1st edition. Actually, I've almost exclusively played 1st edition. By far, my favourite books are Scavenger Sons, Exalted: the Sidereals, and Exalted: the Fair Folk, in that order (Fair Folk would have made 1st place, if not for the Mountain Folk chapter which I found painful). I also like Savant and Sorcerer, Games of Divinity, Manacle and Coin, and Exalted: the Lunars. I really, really dislike Book of Bone and Ebony, and Exalted: the Abyssals; to a lesser extent I also dislike Exalted: the Dragon Blooded and a number of Caste/Aspect books.<br /> <br /> When 2nd edition came out, my game group and I gave it a try and ... well, after a few sessions we decided it wasn't our cup of tea. Mostly because of mechanics we found uselessly convoluted and poorly balanced, but also because of the excessively &quot;animesque&quot; tone -- which admittedly, had been creeping up throughout the second half of the 1st edition line. I gave a glance at a few later supplements and they confirmed my initial opinion. So we went back to playing 1st edition, even though eventually we abandoned it in favour of other games (Blade of the Iron Throne, in particular).<br /> <br /> A few months ago we heard that Exalted 3rd edition had come out, after a loooooong development period -- which we took as a good sign: rushed jobs rarely produce good results. So we decided to give it a new try. We've run just one session with it and so far ... hmmm. It seems definitely much better than 2nd edition. It also seems to solve some, but not all, the problems of 1st edition. And it has a number of smart innovations -- some now almost standard in newer rpgs, some specific to Exalted. It's still a bit rough around the edges though, and has some ugly parts -- like the huge number of different resources one has to track (motes, sorcerous motes, willpower, Intimacy levels, limit, initiative, health levels, xp, solar xp, silver xp, gold xp, white xp ... are we joking?!?). I guess I'll have to play with it a bit more, and see how the rest of the line comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12189-nessuno","user":"nessuno","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12189-nessuno","name":"nessuno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:56:28-07:00","id":944914,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, I'm Broken Masque. I'm a long-time gamer, running the gamut of systems, including RIFTS, D&amp;D, new and old WoD, and of course Exalted.<br /> <br /> I used to be very active around here for a very long time, right back to when 1e was still getting all its splats. It's amusing to think back and remember having all kinds of silly arguments with people back then, some of whom are actually writing the game now! And it's nice to see a lot of the other old faces among the community are still around too.<br /> <br /> Let the obsidian shards rain from the heavens!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:25:53-07:00","id":958160,"title":"","content":"Aha! I can finally post! I see some familiar names including <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz\">Totentanz</a></b>. <br /> <br /> In the original White Wolf forums I was known as Wyrm_Puff. When they got a new forum I used the name I use now, Mal'akh. I was pretty active in the Exalted forums up to the Ex3 kickstarter, but Real Life happened.<br /> <br /> First thing I did upon reading through the whole book was design a Prayer Piece artifact. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:15:58-07:00","id":962217,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. Name's Frishman, been a gamer for eleven years, now. Started with VtR and then moved to D&amp;D (I know, backwards, right?) before playing a little bit of everything anyone would run <i>except</i> Exalted. I got sold on the setting by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> and greedily absorbed all I could to immerse myself, which is why I made a Solar character, a detailed backstory for that character, a detailed backstory for that character's First Age Self, two Artifact histories for that character plus Evocations once I finally got the book, and a short story of how the character met his Lunar mate before he ever Exalted, as told from the Lunar's perspective, including a detailed backstory of that Lunar. Today will be my very first session of any Exalted game, in an online game which my friends and I have been planning to do for close to a year, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:35:50-07:00","id":966174,"title":"","content":"Hello, Alabrax here. Old fan of Exalted but I have ignored it for years. Now I am running a 2nd Ed game again and all the love for the setting is rushing back to me. <br /> <br /> /waves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12392-alabrax","name":"Alabrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:26:37-07:00","id":968072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alabrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=966174#post966174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, Alabrax here. Old fan of Exalted but I have ignored it for years. Now I am running a 2nd Ed game again and all the love for the setting is rushing back to me.<br /> <br /> /waves</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, poster for whom the apocryphal Jadeborn scholar-smith of pre-human 1e thaumaturgy is named. ^(VVVVVVV)^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"tha