"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might be in for a shock in this edition...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much info about Lunars in 3rd. I hope they launch the lunars manual soon. They seem to be afterthought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12585-vanderkrad","name":"Vanderkrad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:44:47-08:00","id":1020018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vanderkrad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1020007#post1020007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much info about Lunars in 3rd. I hope they launch the lunars manual soon. They seem to be afterthought</div> </div> </div> </div>We do have some tidbits beyond the book, between the what we know wiki on avatarcomic and various threads. Such as <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?670878-Exalted-Where-we-speculate-about-Lunar-Exalted-in-Exalted-3rd-edition&amp;p=16307821#post16307821\" target=\"_blank\">this one.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:31:53-08:00","id":1020047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1020018#post1020018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We do have some tidbits beyond the book, between the what we know wiki on avatarcomic and various threads. Such as <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?670878-Exalted-Where-we-speculate-about-Lunar-Exalted-in-Exalted-3rd-edition&amp;p=16307821#post16307821\" target=\"_blank\">this one.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the data!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12585-vanderkrad","name":"Vanderkrad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T03:55:09-08:00","id":1024200,"title":"","content":"Hi all. Been role-playing for 25 years or so. Got into Exalted in the dawn of First Edition and played and ran several very long campaigns over the years until 2e eventually led us to a conscious uncoupling. Very excited for 3e. Just starting a new game now and figuring out how things work again. I used to frequent to old WW Exalted forum but I mostly lurked. I can't actually recall the profile name I used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball","name":"Wizball","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T21:44:16-08:00","id":1024629,"title":"","content":"Hi. I'm Diagrapher. I'm currently a player in a 2ed campaign, and I enjoy coming up with and building characters, comparing editions, trying to find holes in the charm sets, hearing about different takes on Exalted's setting and potential stories and coming up with my own, and various other things to do with exalted. I love the structuredness of certain things in Exalted- how each sort of Exalt corresponds to a magical material and each element a direction and so forth. And while 3ed definitely looks like it will be an improvement on 2ed in at least some ways, I don't like how the 3ed developers are so negative about 2ed- 2ed is still a pretty good game IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:50:56-08:00","id":1029405,"title":"","content":"Hey all. I'm Libaros, and have been putting off posting anything around here for far to long. I've been playing tabletops for about 4 years now, and started to run games this last 4 months or so (choosing Exalted to start my career as a DM has been a small mistake). I am playing in a ongoing 3e game and running a 3e with players all new to the system, so its a learning experience all around. I enjoy making artifacts and deities in most systems, but abhor stating them. I've creeped about the forums for a while now, so now that I have stuff to share I hope to get to know some of you well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Enjoy the moment with all your might,<br /> Whether its gloomy, whether its bright.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12786-libaros","name":"Libaros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:17:48-08:00","id":1038731,"title":"","content":"Hey all! I used to be very active on previous versions of the forums, and elsewhere, as Magnificentmomo. I fell off for awhile between editions (after backing the KS), and lost some steam so wasn't active during the Ex3 go live. I've been recently reintroduced and reinvigorated and loving this new edition (if you hadn't already noticed my activity). I'd have to say it was Exaltwitch and Doom and Gloam that finally got me to jump into 3e (I was kinda waiting for my Deluxe Edition, but I don't want to start that conversation).<br /> <br /> So hello again my old friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T08:44:37-08:00","id":1061256,"title":"","content":"Hello World!<br /> I\u2019m a history student as well as a hobby artist and conlanger. I\u2019ve been playing Exalted with my micro-group for quite some time now. I hope to find new ideas and inspirations for our game(s) and meet interesting people on this forum.<br /> Sadly my English is not the best when writing or speaking, but my understanding of it is quite good. Please forgive me the mistakes I may make in the future and feel free to point them out to me.<br /> <br /> And in the case you are wondering what<span style=\"color:#000000\"> \u201c</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">iri </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">iri\u201d</span> means, it\u2019s the sound of frying tempura. <span style=\"color:#000000\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13115-piri-piri","user":"Piri-Piri","date":". 03-11-2017, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13115-piri-piri","name":"Piri-Piri","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:32:36-07:00","id":1066219,"title":"","content":"Huh, I never posted here, it seems.<br /> <br /> Hi. I'm Weimann. I'm a very-soon-to-be thirty-something from Sweden, where I teach Swedish (to native speakers) and English (as a second language) on the Swedish equivalent of high school level (which for reference is called &quot;gymnasium&quot;, much to the confusion of English-speakers).<br /> <br /> I've been into Exalted since... sometime after Infernals and before Ink Monkeys? Like many, I love the setting, but I've had very little opportunity to actually play the game. My goal now is to get something going once Terrestrials 3e hits, by force if I have to. I'm currently slowly indoctrinating my friends into RPGs through Dungeon World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:50:03-07:00","id":1066304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1066219#post1066219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I never posted here, it seems.<br /> <br /> Hi. I'm Weimann. I'm a very-soon-to-be thirty-something from Sweden, where I teach Swedish (to native speakers) and English (as a second language) on the Swedish equivalent of high school level (which for reference is called &quot;gymnasium&quot;, much to the confusion of English-speakers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, this English speaker is definitely confused, though as a Texan I have experienced many public high schools that are really just elaborate gyms for football teams.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:07:02-07:00","id":1066416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1066304#post1066304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, this English speaker is definitely confused, though as a Texan I have experienced many public high schools that are really just elaborate gyms for football teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>It stems from the same root etymologically. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnasium_(ancient_Greece)\" target=\"_blank\">From Wikipedia</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The word </span></span></span><i>gymnasium</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latinisation_(literature)\" target=\"_blank\">latinisation</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> of the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_language\" target=\"_blank\">Greek</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> noun \u03b3\u03c5\u03bc\u03bd\u03ac\u03c3\u03b9\u03bf\u03bd (</span></span></span><i>gymnasion</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">), &quot;gymnastic school&quot;, in pl. &quot;bodily exercises&quot; and generally &quot;school&quot;</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnasium_%28ancient_Greece%29#cite_note-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> which in turn is derived from the common Greek adjective </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%CE%B3%CF%85%CE%BC%CE%BD%CF%8C%CF%82#Ancient_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">\u03b3\u03c5\u03bc\u03bd\u03cc\u03c2</a></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (</span></span></span><i>gymnos</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">) meaning &quot;naked&quot;,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnasium_%28ancient_Greece%29#cite_note-3\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> by way of the related verb \u03b3\u03c5\u03bc\u03bd\u03ac\u03b6\u03c9 (</span></span></span><i>gymnazo</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">), whose meaning is &quot;to train naked&quot;, &quot;train in gymnastic exercise&quot;, generally &quot;to train, to exercise&quot;.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gymnasium_%28ancient_Greece%29#cite_note-4\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The verb had this meaning because one undressed for exercise. Historically, the gymnasium was used for exercise, communal </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathing\" target=\"_blank\">bathing</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and scholarly and </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">philosophical</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> pursuits.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>During the 1500s, the word &quot;gymnasium&quot; started to be used in Germany to refer to schools giving education that prepared for university, which is how it's used in Sweden today. Later, however, we also imported the English meaning in the shortened form &quot;gym&quot;, so when someone says &quot;jag g\u00e5r till gymmet&quot; (I'm going to the gym), they do mean they're going to perform physical exercise, not that they're off to school.<br /> <br /> Although, &quot;gym&quot; doesn't mean quite the same thing in English and Swedish either. In English, I'm given to understand that it can refer to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Calhan_Colorado_High_School_Gymnasium_by_David_Shankbone.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">big open indoor hall</a> or outdoor field where any exercise or sport can be practiced, as well as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Crossfit_gym_cz.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">spaces with machines, barbells and more stationary workout equipment</a>. In Swedish, a &quot;gym&quot; is specifically the latter; a place for workout machines and equipment. You'd never, for example, play football in a gym, but you'd perhaps do it in the &quot;gymnastiksal&quot; (&quot;gymnastics hall&quot;), which fits more with the former meaning.<br /> <br /> We're also not typically naked in any of these situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-22-2017, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:17:09-07:00","id":1066786,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit late posting here, but Hi! I'm M. InkSplatterM if you want to get formal. I can be found in the greater Chicagoland area of the US. Been interested in Exalted since I found it about midway through it's second edition (you could still buy the books in bookstores and I thiiiiink that at least up to the DB book was published), when I found it and other (then) white wolf publishing games. <br /> <br /> I'm mostly interested in sliding the things I homebrew by other people becuase I have a never ending need for validation, and I'm always nervous about if the mechanics are balanced okay enough. <br /> <br /> Glad to be here though and I really like reading the conversations in other threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:28:04-07:00","id":1067350,"title":"","content":"Hello! I joined a while ago but this would be my first post here, please excuse the tardiness. I got into Exalted sometime after the last few books were rolled out for 2E. Since the arrival of the much anticipated 3E, I've played several oneshot short arc campaigns with my friends. We sometimes play Changeling as well.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to stumble across ideas for character building and homebrew, errata, and maybe participate in a few quests. (I... sorta lurked on wonderandawe's Hero. It was great!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12389-pelleas","name":"Pelleas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:01:33-07:00","id":1070615,"title":"","content":"I am a cop by training, and in two weeks I will be returning to police work in a small town just outside Manhattan, Kansas. I am a married guy with two very small boys. I am just over 40 and I have been playing RPGs since I was 11 in boy scouts.<br /> <br /> I got into Exalted during the Power Combat era of 1st edition. The forum was a nasty place back then. We said nasty stuff and treated each other poorly. I am too damn old for that now.<br /> <br /> Why do I tell folks I am a cop? Well, it informs how I look at the world. Words in statutes mean some specific things. It can make me literal minded, and sometimes that is good. Other times bad. It also means that I write differently when trying to figure out what folks mean.<br /> <br /> I am very happy to be back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:23:20-07:00","id":1070659,"title":"","content":"Oh, I haven't done this either. Let's share!<br /> <br /> I live in Sweden, on the east-coast, in a town known for burning goats. I work in customer service for a train company because I can't find a better job. I have used our free education system to study professional writing, journalism and philosophy, but I got lazy and never finished a degree. So I got stuck with customer service for now with plans to go back to school before I get too old. As I'm writing this, I'm starting to get too old. I'm 29 years old and closing in on 30. I'm a dude and my forum name means Squirrel in Swedish. Squirrels are awesome animals and we need a badass squirrel Lunar as a 3E canon character.<br /> <br /> The first time I played a tabletop roleplaying game was when I was eight years old and my older neighbor had this Swedish game called &quot;Drakar och demoner&quot;. I didn't understand anything at the time, but I was hooked, and I spent the ages 8 to 10 to try to write my own roleplaying game because my older neighbor didn't want to play anymore. Since I didn't know anything about rpg systems when I was 8, I ended up drawing pictures of axes in a notepad, and then smugly tell people around me that I was a serious game designer. When I was 10, I bought my own rpg book for a Swedish game called Eon. What I didn't know at the time was that Eon is a game with an unnecessarily complex system, having convoluted mechanics for every single thing you can think of. Not the game to get when you're 10. I did learn how to make characters though. Since I had no friends interested in the hobby, I spent ages 10-15 making characters and writing stories for this one game I never played. Then I put the books away, introduced myself to emo culture, and became the most pretentious little poet imaginable. I did meet girls though, so it wasn't all bad.<br /> <br /> Age 18, got into a writing school, and started hanging out with nerds again. Lo and behold, these nerds played roleplaying games. When I was 19, a friend asked me &quot;Do you want to play Exalted?&quot; I said: &quot;I used to play stuff like that when I was a kid&quot; (even though I never actually played as a kid). So we had our first session of Exalted. That first character I made is still my favorite character and he is also my profile picture. I was hooked immediately.<br /> <br /> Now I've invested most of my free time for ten years doing something Exalted related, like storytelling, playing or making custom content. I don't see myself stopping any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T14:15:44-07:00","id":1072694,"title":"","content":"So.. Hi! I'm five days away from being an 24 year old dude who drives a taxi for a living from Finland. I live in a small town smack in the middle of nowhere with my girlfriend and our daughter. I'd also like to once again mention - and possibly apologize in advance - that I'm not a native English speaker so if I've somehow managed to already offend someone, it most likely has been non-intentional. Probably. Maybe.<br /> <br /> I've actually been an anonymous lurker for years now, even back in the days when those white wolf forums were still up and running, and only just recently bothered to actually register - with Exalted 3rd edition being one of the primary motivators for me to do so. I've had very poor luck so I haven't actually played 3rd edition yet - and not for a lack of trying - but I'm hoping 3rd ed Dragonbloods will change that. Besides that, I've got some experience in primarily playing several of the World of Darkness splats, both old and new with a healthy mix of Scion. Of all of those games, Exalted is actually my favourite - terrestrials and infernals in particular - even though I've unfortunately got very little experience in actually playing it. I'm currently searching for a ST and players interested in playing Exalted with me over the internet, so if anyone interested reads this, feel free to contact me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11765-dominuete","name":"Dominuete","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T00:03:00-07:00","id":1074035,"title":"","content":"Hello from Korea. =O I first started playing Exalted 13-ish years ago and I was kinda active on the old forum, but I fell off and only recently got back into Exalted. I've gotten a local group together and I figured getting feedback on my ideas and sharing my homebrew stuff would be nice.<br /> <br /> I guess one thing to note is that I'm in the process of translating Exalted stuff slowly -- playing Exalted with non-English speakers kinda made that necessary and once I used classical literary wuxia terms for Exalted-specific words, I had to do the whole thing in the style. If anyone's interested in reading about my translation process, let me know. I'd love to share what I've gotten down (as far as copyright laws and RPG content-sharing conventions would permit, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T00:34:38-07:00","id":1074044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>szp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1074035#post1074035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess one thing to note is that I'm in the process of translating Exalted stuff slowly -- playing Exalted with non-English speakers kinda made that necessary and once I used classical literary wuxia terms for Exalted-specific words, I had to do the whole thing in the style. If anyone's interested in reading about my translation process, let me know. I'd love to share what I've gotten down (as far as copyright laws and RPG content-sharing conventions would permit, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. I almost exclusively play English RPGs with my RL groups. There are plenty of Swedish RPGs around, but we want to play our favorites instead and they are all in English: Exalted, Cyberpunk 2020, D&amp;D. It gets kind of interesting how you communicate in Swedish and then add random &quot;Swedishification&quot; of English words from the game just to make the sentences coherent. It's even more interesting when there isn't a consensus and players start mixing even more, with some having characters bearing English names and others have characters with Swedish names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T01:02:00-07:00","id":1074052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1074044#post1074044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting. I almost exclusively play English RPGs with my RL groups. There are plenty of Swedish RPGs around, but we want to play our favorites instead and they are all in English: Exalted, Cyberpunk 2020, D&amp;D. It gets kind of interesting how you communicate in Swedish and then add random &quot;Swedishification&quot; of English words from the game just to make the sentences coherent. It's even more interesting when there isn't a consensus and players start mixing even more, with some having characters bearing English names and others have characters with Swedish names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I can imagine how that could work. But I think it's much harder to do that in Korean, though. Exalted has a very strong wuxia feel, but using English to describe such things kinda conflicts with Korean gamers' pre-existing ideas of wuxia, I think. Language and RPG in Korea have always had a weird deal. When talking about short, bearded, cave-dwelling, ale-drinking dwarves in fantasy RPGs, Korean gamers use the transliteration \ub4dc\uc6cc\ud504 rather than the Korean word \ub09c\uc7c1\uc774. It just feels... more &quot;fantastic&quot; to us. Or something. I wish I could elaborate further on this, but I'm kinda delirious from sleep deprivation. =d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:40:49-07:00","id":1075123,"title":"","content":"So contributing to this shindig:<br /> <br /> I'm Blaque. I first started with RPGs back in 2000 with <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>. Since then I've played or run that, <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>, <b>D&amp;D</b> (3.5e, 4e and 5e), <b>Shadowrun </b>(3e and 4e), <b>Dresdon Files</b>, <b>Scion</b>, <b>Adventure!</b>, <b>Don't Rest Your Head</b>, <b>In a WIcked Age</b>, <b>BESM</b> (I even have playtest credits in 3e), <b>Legends of the Wulin</b>, <b>Legend of the Five Rings</b> and of course, <b>Exalted</b>.<br /> <br /> I got into <b>Exalted </b>when it came out though with 1e, got hyped when they first announced it and it has been my main game since. I've ran multiple campaigns over the years, though rarely ever have gotten to play, in all Directions and even I think for most splats save Sidereals (no one ever wanted to play one in my games) and Fair Folk (too much a pain in the ass).<br /> <br /> For not-Exalted or RPG stuff, I like science, technology, politics, philosophy (I'm in a philosophy PhD program currently), history, anime and manga, cartoons in general, sci-fi and fantasy fiction and other pretty standard nerd shit. I draw cartoony fantasy art, often inspired by Exalted you <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">can find here</a> if you haven't seen it yet and <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/blog/blaqueandstuff\" target=\"_blank\">have a blog</a> I tossed-up not long ago to try and get more of a &quot;how I do this&quot; thing going. Might move it though to something like a Squarespace site if I can get more stuff on there this summer.<br /> <br /> And I'm also known for ending all my posts with &quot;And stuff.&quot; This is the result of the old WW forums originally having you have to write your signature sby-hand since they used awful old shitty software. It's now become almost a compulsive tick when I finish a post. So yeah, deal with it.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:50:40-07:00","id":1075629,"title":"","content":"Finally got my profile approved. Yay.<br /> So I think my handle speaks for itself(no...me, a Zelda fan? Whatever gave you that idea?). I got into Exalted 1e as a result of joining a VtM game way back in 2002 or so...been mainly tabletopping that ever since. In fact, Blaque was the guy who introduced me to Exalted all those years ago. Amusing timing that he posted in here right when I'm finally able to. So hey, big kudos and thanks to him.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm learning the ins and outs of 3e, having to home brew a &quot;2.75&quot; for a game I'm getting started that's primarily Dragon-Blooded, being they're my favorite type(go House V'neef), and in general getting back into Creation after a few years away. I'm pretty sure 3e finally coming out helped that, and very eagerly awaiting the future splits. Especially my Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently homebrewing &quot;<b>Dragon-Blooded 2.75</b>&quot; system.<br /> <br /> Games currently running: <b><a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=47166\" target=\"_blank\">The Throne of Ice</a> - RPoL</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13131-heroofhylia","name":"Heroofhylia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13131_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:23:52-07:00","id":1075676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofhylia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1075629#post1075629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got my profile approved. Yay.<br /> So I think my handle speaks for itself(no...me, a Zelda fan? Whatever gave you that idea?). I got into Exalted 1e as a result of joining a VtM game way back in 2002 or so...been mainly tabletopping that ever since. In fact, Blaque was the guy who introduced me to Exalted all those years ago. Amusing timing that he posted in here right when I'm finally able to. So hey, big kudos and thanks to him.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm learning the ins and outs of 3e, having to home brew a &quot;2.75&quot; for a game I'm getting started that's primarily Dragon-Blooded, being they're my favorite type(go House V'neef), and in general getting back into Creation after a few years away. I'm pretty sure 3e finally coming out helped that, and very eagerly awaiting the future splits. Especially my Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, you should check out Crumplepunch's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\">Clutch of Dragons</a> Homebrew, which provides a healthy amount of options for playing DBs in 3e until the book comes out.<br /> <br /> Welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:04:49-07:00","id":1075692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1075676#post1075676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If nothing else, you should check out Crumplepunch's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\">Clutch of Dragons</a> Homebrew, which provides a healthy amount of options for playing DBs in 3e until the book comes out.<br /> <br /> Welcome!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, and I actually have that thread subscribed to! The hardest thing is we started originally in 2e with ink monkey Errata, and there's a hodgepodge of bits from both old and new. It's being run mainly on RPoL, so mechanics aren't super heavy, but it's still been interesting, especially since I like to run higher power games. I know as I delve more and more into 3e, it'll get easier to work it out down the road, probably when I do a Solar based story group down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently homebrewing &quot;<b>Dragon-Blooded 2.75</b>&quot; system.<br /> <br /> Games currently running: <b><a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=47166\" target=\"_blank\">The Throne of Ice</a> - RPoL</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13131-heroofhylia","name":"Heroofhylia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13131_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:03:47-07:00","id":1075937,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, my name is <b>Norr</b>, and unfortunately i'm not as consistent as some others on here apparently so this is just one of many usernames i've used since getting online at the age of 11. On the old forums i think my name might have been <b>bootnorr</b>, but it's hard to remember.<br /> <br /> I started RPing in highschool when a friend invited me to their online dragon riders of pern rpg, but i started playing tabletop rpg's about when i was 23, so 6 years ago. Since then i have played exalted off and on, as well as 40k rogue trader, star wars edge of the empire, warhammer fantasy rpg, dnd 3.5 and 5th, legend of the five rings, vampire, scion, and a few more that escape me at the moment and a few more i'm starting soon but haven't played yet.<br /> Most of this time has been spent as a player, despite fluff and world building being one of my favorite part of all the games, it has been difficult for me in the past to figure out how to incorporate my fellow players into the story i'm hoping to tell, which is the problem actually since they should be the ones telling the story while i provide the setting lol.<br /> <br /> About exalted i would have to say that my favorite thing would be the crafting, which took me so much by surprise since i could not even understand the crafting rules in the previous edition, and i spend a lot of time just thinking about what to craft in game and shooting ideas back and forth with my ST on how to do things. In fact i think most of the posts i made on this forum a ways back before i went ghost again were related to crafting.<br /> <br /> as for non game related stuff:<ul><li>i am an educator, having worked with preschool to elementary aged children for the past 7 years and it's something i greatly enjoy and hope to keep doing for a long time.</li> <li>I am a second generation palestinian christian immigrant, my wife is palestinian muslim, and my cultural background and my own peoples struggle has an impact on a lot of a lot of my opinions.</li> <li>I have my undergrad with my areas of study being asian studies, anthropology, and middle east and islamic studies.</li> <li>I'm hoping to pursue masters in education and palestinian studies and inshallah one day a doctorate in conflict resolution studies with a focus on how education can be used to help solve ethnic conflict.</li> </ul>Sorry if it's a bit much about my job in education or my own plans for my education, but my interests are pretty much in the lines of reading, writing, learning, and helping and educating others, with one last thing being that i am also a SJW (Though i prefer social justice bard class) and a socialist, which i only mention because it does effect my game play, in as much as much of a way that my character is currently trying to eliminate poverty, hunger, and al forms of inequality in chiaroscuro, and due to what foxy said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899158#post899158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ol' Foxy enjoys pro wrestling and is an unabashed Social Justice Warrior, which is a term we should wear with pride because it sounds fucking awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>anyway thats me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T06:40:59-07:00","id":1081416,"title":"","content":"Whoof. Did I really put this off so long?<br /> <br /> Welp, I'm Arian Dynas, and before you ask, no, it was an ill-conceived name picked out of a character generation book, not some kind of comment. I've gone by that handle for quite a while now, it was the name of a D&amp;D character I made but never did play, mostly because I was a lonely preteen, and when I did actually get to play D&amp;D as a kid, I was always the DM.<br /> <br /> I'm a prospective writer who's just graduated from College, I live in Alaska, and no, it's not really as cold as you'd think. I'm an anthropologist and philosopher, or at least that's what my degree says, and simply put; I freaking love Exalted. I've loved RPGs since I was 5 years old, watching my big brothers sitting at a table, sometimes playing AD&amp;D, sometimes Space-Hulk. I actually got to playing about in middle school. I keep a big ol library of RPG books in my apartment; friends have been concerned that an earthquake may well crush me under falling bookshelves.<br /> <br /> I'm also one half of the dev team for an Exalted character generator and manager, Anathema Reincarnated, if you're interested in that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> In my case I discovered Exalted through World of Darkness; I'd been reading a Ghenna scenario in which it said one of the possible outcomes would be an &quot;Exalted&quot; like setting. Having a vague frame of reference based on a TV tropes article about &quot;Always Chaotic Evil&quot; demons being justified in setting, I talked it over with the friend I was plotting out this massive Ghenna scenario with, and we figured we'd try Exalted as the result of the players winning the Ghenna scenario. Aaaaaand that was when we first fell down the rabbit hole. I picked up a copy of the 2e manual in a used bookstore and was deeply intrigued; we decided to give it a crack sometime, so I read up, discovered Keychain of Creation, and was pretty well in by this point, but, something was wrong. Basically, Second Edition burned me multiple times on what I saw was a wonderful idea.<br /> <br /> It didn't help that at the time I had a friend who was *way* into Second Edition and took everything as gospel; including all of the fluff that John Morke would have termed &quot;Shitdark&quot; so for a while, everything that I got excited for in setting, and mechanics wise, it'd get shot down. This culminated in when I read DotFA, and although I was clinging to a love for it, the magic was gone. Maybe it was a sunk-cost fallacy on my part.<br /> <br /> Then I heard about EX3. I read some stuff; I got excited. I started clearing out some old assumptions 2e had engendered in me, then, I read Richard Danksy's Trilogy of the Second Age. The last two books... weren't that good, but the first one... even with a disappointing ending, the book opened my mind again, so many things that were boxed and labelled, forced into specific unchanging roles in my mind about Exalted suddenly burst out again, just because of the way that Exalted's first Dev wrote about it.I started reading 1e books, and suddenly, the magic was back! There wasn't much of it, but everything was so evocative and powerful again and I felt I could grow to love it again that it didn't matter that there wasn't nearly as much of the passion as before.<br /> <br /> Then 3e came out, and I loved it; it seemed to be a fulfillment of all of the promises that I'd been given the first time I'd heard the name &quot;Exalted&quot; Something was still missing though... then I read Tales from the Flat Earth, and everything just clicked. Conan, Anime, Western Fantasy, Ghibli Movies, The Bible and bullshit Wuxia Demigods suddenly all crystallized. And now, here I am.<br /> <br /> I'll be stomping these forums mostly for the fun of it, and to share a passion with you all, so I'll catch you on the flip side.<br /> <br /> Oh and in case anybody knows me from the Bioware Forums, I have a tendency for Walls-O-Text. I'm told I got rather infamous for it there.<br /> <br /> Oh and for the people who care about that sort of thing, since I'm an anthropologist, the big reason I love Exalted, especially now, is not just the bullshit Kung-Fu Demigods, but also the deep down verisimilitude of the setting, along with it's kitchen sink tendencies. So being an Anthro, my political leanings tend toward the egalitarian, liberal, and generally treating everyone with compassion. For those of you who care to know that sort of thing, as I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":2442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","user":"Arian Dynas","date":". 04-20-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:01:38-07:00","id":1084464,"title":"","content":"Hello I am Smasmaster. (or just Smas\u2026it was a catchy and unique name that fit and just caught on over time)<br /> <br /> I have been playing tabletop RPGs since my first cleric in the D&amp;D Red Box in Fourth Grade. From there it was the various Palladium games (TMNT, Robotech, their fantasy setting, Rifts, so on and so forth)\u2026then, later on, it was Shadowrun Second Edition\u2026and then back to D&amp;D 4th, 5th, and a very healthy dose of Pathfinder. (Currently playing a wizard in a Kingmaker game that has been running for just over three years now). <br /> <br /> (Warning I am fond of using lots of parenthesis and ellipses in my writing...ENGLISH GRAMMAR BE DAMNED)<br /> <br /> I have been a collector of various RPGs over the years of games I games I would love to play but never got a chance to (see Nobilis, The One Ring, and a long list of others). Exalted was one of these games\u2026I love, love, love the setting and idea that the PCs are uber powerful and can change the world\u2026that aspect which I feel was unique to all Role Playing Games at the time it came out. I love the different types of Exalted and how they interact and their flavors. <br /> <br /> I, unfortunately, had to sell my whole Exalted 2nd Edition collection years ago (family needs &gt; gaming)\u2026when I thought i would never get to play. And then while lurking on <a href=\"http://RPG.net\" target=\"_blank\">RPG.net</a> I discovered the absolutely amazingly well played and written story \u201cTen Thousand Broken Dreams\u201d \u2026and I got the itch again. But could not find a group a the time\u2026and let it pass.<br /> <br /> And now recently when I heard that the 3rd edition was out and developed by the very author and GM of that amazing story who has a presence on these very boards..so I revisited the story on <a href=\"http://RPG.net\" target=\"_blank\">RPG.net</a> again\u2026and now have the itch once more. <br /> <br /> Things had changed in my life since those last few times and now I may\u2026have some potential players for my own story of Exalted\u2026although I would love to play in a group (and if anyone has a space available via Roll20 or some online method for a player I would be interested.) So I hope to plan on participating here and hopefully running Exalted in some way shape or form in the near future.<br /> <br /> I live in Ohio. I am a father of two future players of RPGs\u2026married to a woman I converted into a gamer for over twenty years now. I am a Biomedical Data Analyst by trade\u2026with a liberal arts degree in Political Science and History. I play the Viola, I love music and have a very eclectic taste in it. I read lots, play computer and Xbox games (right now it is Starcraft 2 Coop with my son), watch various sci fi shows and movies (Dr. Who, Star Wars in all of its incarnations, Steven Universe, and the Expanse..the list goes on), I am a die-hard National Hockey League fan and write quite a bit\u2026mainly back and forth RP emailing with friends and some of my own fantasy stories, and drink lots of wine.<br /> <br /> &lt;waves to everyone&gt;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13295-smasmaster","name":"smasmaster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T09:31:23-07:00","id":1086223,"title":"","content":"Huzzah, I am approved!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am Voyd. I'm a complete and total geekazoid.<br /> <br /> I'm relatively new to tabletop games (I only started playing two or three years ago, and Pathfinder is still the only one I've played), but I'm very eager to try a few new ones... namely Exalted.<br /> <br /> I've been reading, watching movies, and playing video games as long as I can remember.<br /> <br /> As far as Exalted, uh... all of the sources I have access to are for 2E, so that's what I'm mostly interested in discussing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:37:20-07:00","id":1086835,"title":"","content":"Greetings, I am Ben, feel free to stick to the forum name though. Aside from my forum name, I've been known as Rykon, Grifnir, Renost, Berdain, and a number of other names on the internet. I was born and raised in Tennessee and currently approaching my late 20s.<br /> <br /> Additional context for those interested... I've earned a Bachelors of Science Degree in Computer Science, Accounting, and Finance from the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga. I am currently working as a contracted Software Engineer in the energy industry by day. I've also started an online business that I build up in the evenings and on weekends, in an effort to help out the family as my parent's (and my own) retirement prospects seem dim.<br /> <br /> I got introduced to Exalted at what I believe was the very end of 2E by a classmate and dear friend that was running a game of Deadlands on campus. Ever since I've been helplessly enthralled by the game, to the extent that other white wolf properties fail to sell me on spending the time with them in spite of their charm. Picking a favorite splat is very difficult for me, but at the moment I am most excited about Dragon-Blooded seeing how it's the one I've never gotten close to playing. So far my most memorable characters are 2 different Eclipse castes, a Zenith caste, and a Journey's Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Outside of Exalted, I've been blessed with a group that's running a whole host of different pen and paper games. However, video games are my primary hobby. My favorite genres are Adventure and Role Playing with a bit of an aversion to FPS games and MOBAs. Non-gaming hobbies include anime, manga, and leisurely sketching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T20:10:28-07:00","id":1093074,"title":"","content":"Hello. New to the forum and only semi new to exalted. I first played 2nd ed back in 2011 or so and had a lot of fun (Night caste merchant who wanted to command the guild). Now I am running a 3rd ed game over skype and taking them all over the place. I am hoping to get some advice on custom stuff, like artifacts, custom charms and even combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Nobody ever expects the immaculate inquisition!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13386-brambleclaw","name":"Brambleclaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T14:26:22-07:00","id":1095620,"title":"","content":"Hi. My name is Dexter though my screen name or Dex will suffice. Call me what you want. I am a soon to be college student from Florida who wants to get into video game design (though the revelations from games like Exalted and Shadowrun may possibly change my aspirations).<br /> <br /> I'm a happy addition to the Exalted gaming community by only about 2 years meaning I really only learned of the game as 3E was getting pushed. I have been into tabletop gaming for an only marginally longer time of about 3 years. It started with a friend dragging me into his homebrew RPG and then another player introduced me to Exalted and the Eastern and Wuxia nature of the game pulled me in like a black hole. I also have thought of playing aShadowrun campaign but have not had a chance to yet. Lunars are probably my favorite splat with the Sidereals and Abyssals quickly following. I don't particularly find the Solars an interesting group but then again, I've never played a Solar and this may possibly skew my view of many aspects of the game. I have played in two games of Exalted. One, a heavily homebrewed edition of 2E that ended in disaster due to player infighting. I am now playing a 2.5 series where we keep more to the book and we're a bit better for it. I am planning a one-shot game of 3E though (probably a foolish idea, but I dare to attempt it anyways) and may or may not request help from the forums when stymied.<br /> <br /> I as a person I am a bit dull and it may take me a bit to understand an introduced idea or concept. As such I may occasionally ask for something to be broken down to me. I've also never played an offline game so that may color my perceptions a bit differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13053-dxzstar","name":"Dxzstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13053_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T16:48:24-07:00","id":1095657,"title":"","content":"I'm Tytalus.<br /> <br /> I got into RPGs at the tender age of 12 with Steve Jackson's Advanced Fighting Fantasy books &quot;Dungeoneer&quot;, &quot;Blacksand&quot; and &quot;Titan&quot;. I loved those books and used them until they were shredded. I moved on to Ars Magic and V:tM for a number of years before picking up Mage:the Sorceror's Crusade, and then Mage:the Ascension.<br /> <br /> In the Summer of 2003 I discovered Exalted and it's been a long on again off again love hate relationship where I keep coming back no matter how much I'm abused. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:35:34-07:00","id":1097020,"title":"","content":"Hi I'm Nightshrike,<br /> <br /> Long-time lurker, now occasional poster. I picked up First Ed just over 10 years ago but never got to play it. Now I share storytelling duties in a semi-regular game that's been running for about 5 years on and off. We started playing on Second Ed and have since upgraded to Third.<br /> <br /> The lore of exalted has always been the biggest drawing point for me. I first started tabletop playing V:TM with friends in high school and I got hooked on the idea of Exalted being the pre-history of oWoD.<br /> <br /> The last thing to mention is that I hail from that great land Down Under. So, if you reply to me and I don't answer I'm not being rude, just being asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6585-nightshrike","name":"nightshrike","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T11:15:57-07:00","id":1098489,"title":"","content":"So, not sure if anyone reads these things but making sure I say hi before jumping into things seems right and proper <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm andrix, lurked for years and managed to hold off on making an account, probably because I'm not sure I've had anything worth saying. I'm a member of Lioness' gaming group however, including being a player in her long running game, and between them they've peer pressured me into signing up to add to the volume of art and stories that gets shared around. So she's entirely liable for me. I also run a weekly game for the same group with some (most?) of the player characters already shared on here.<br /> <br /> I've been playing since way back in 1e when all we had was a corebook and storytellers guide, played pretty frequently through the majority of 2e and was a playtester for 3e. While most of my playtime is online I've also got a small RL group which has a semi-frequent D&amp;D 5e game and spend more money than they should on MTG","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13512-andrix","user":"andrix","date":". 05-30-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13512-andrix","name":"andrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T04:31:39-07:00","id":1101560,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Canis. <br /> <br /> I'm another mostly-lurking type but I'm trying to break free of the conditioned response that the Exalted forums are a scary, scary place. I got my start to Exalted in 2nd ed, but I just got EX3 a couple of weeks ago and I'm still nosing my way through it. <br /> <br /> My name, of course, is a tribute to a character I played on an Exalted chat a number of years ago who happened to be a God-blooded dog (I don't think Scroll of Heroes is speaking to me after what I put it through to make that work). On a <i>completely unrelated</i> note, I am patiently awaiting Exigents. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13529-canisinvictus","name":"CanisInvictus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T03:11:21-07:00","id":1112587,"title":"","content":"Hiya, I'm Slovorg<br /> Another lurker trying to become more social. I'm a swedish hotel worker with too much spare time and way to active of an imagination. Having spent more time than I'd like to admit on moderation free parts of the internet I am trying my bet to be polite and constructive and not yell obscenities at people. I enjoy discussions, logical conclusions and breaking RPG systems and then fixing them, also known as house-ruling. <br /> <br /> Roleplaying wise I am of the opinion that a well understood system is never a limitation to narrative elements and that any good system can simulate everything with a competent ST at the head of it. The most important aspects are fun, immersion and challenge, in that order. My characters tend to the violent sort, but are almost always the last to resort to violence. Figuring out peaceful resolutions and compromises at first and encouraging political shenanigans as a second. Wholesale slaughter as a third. It's always good to have a backup. <br /> <br /> I am looking forwad to lunars, dragon-blooded and infernals. I enjoy making typical antagonists into heroes. <br /> <br /> As a storyteller I am a world builder. I craft settings in the empty spaces between fluff and make something of my own among the old. My campaigns are long, needlessly complicated and very sandbox. The players are the primary agents of change, and this is why I love exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T10:39:59-07:00","id":1113287,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! I'm Roswynn (or Ros, Rose, Rosie, &quot;Hey you!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). My name comes from a genius artificer I played in D&amp;D 4e, who grabbed my heart and ran away with it, and since then she's been by far my favourite alias (in Exalted she's a Twilight from Ironfall).<br /> <br /> English isn't my first language so I hope I won't make too many glaring mistakes, fingers crossed.<br /> <br /> I love being the ST (or DM, or GM...) because it means I get to take a little corner of the game world and fill it with cool people and things for my players to interact with, and I love what my players can come up with.<br /> <br /> All 2 of them (we're very old friends and we have a special chemistry at the table).<br /> <br /> Lately I've more often run premade D&amp;D 5e campaigns for them, with some success, but I've known Exalted since First Edition came out and it has always intrigued me. The rules, on the other hand, well...<br /> <br /> When 3e appeared I tried my hand at running it, but I ended up abandoning the experiment in frustration at the system's complexity (some people say I'm smart, but I'm not sure I believe them).<br /> <br /> I tried looking for an alternate system - but even though some might be used to run an approximation of Exalted, I believe the original ruleset is just the best at really conveying the actual flavor of the setting, surprising absolutely no one.<br /> <br /> So I decided to give it another try (and I'm *really* trying hard to learn it well enough), because I love Creation and the Exalted, and all the lore I've read since I was a little girl. My players are game. So wish me luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T09:24:43-07:00","id":1116432,"title":"","content":"&quot;Always an ST, never a player...&quot;<br /> <br /> Hey all, I go by Balbary (named after my favorite Solar character I played in 1st Edition). I've been running games for over 15 years, starting with Aberrant and moving to Exalted and Pathfinder. Exalted will always be my absolute favorite setting. <br /> <br /> With 3rd edition I've been adding a lot of uncommon elements to my games like using playing cards printed with character art instead of minis, an initiative tracking mat with poker chips marking each character, and physical coins to actually keep track of money (bucking the traditional Resources mechanic).<br /> <br /> My games are heavily improvised often with just a few scrawled notes to set the framework. They also have been skewing toward the lighthearted side (a la Fairy Tail) with my current group and that's totally fine.<br /> <br /> I'm also a lurker and don't post very often, but have been working on a new Exalted project lately and wanted to share with the forum, so I'll hopefully be posting that in a few days. <br /> <br /> So... hi!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2884-balbary","name":"Balbary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2884_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T12:24:55-07:00","id":1137397,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I first got my hands on Exalted about 6-7 years ago. GM:ed a few groups but non that really stuck together for too long.<br /> <br /> I really fell in love with the setting because of the basic premise of &quot;the world is doomed and everything is stacked against you and you might just as well give up... If it were not for the fact that you are a SOLAR EXALTED, CHOSEN OF THE UNCONQUERED SUN&quot;. I really like the idea of the characters being empowered to actually change the world.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I live in Sweden and recently started GM:ing Third Edition with my friends!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I SHOOT THE GIGGLING!... What do I know about &quot;giggling&quot;?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1089-captainsl","name":"CaptainSL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1089_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T03:16:01-08:00","id":1161461,"title":"","content":"I'm Illaden and I'm from Sweden and live in a small town called Kosta :P <br /> <br /> I'm mostly just an RPG fan. Playing most of the RPG video/pc games that comes out and have been playing tabletop for 12 years now. <br /> The tabletop rpg I have been playing is mostly the Swedish rpg EON and after that it has been &quot;Mutant heir of the fall&quot; or in Swedish Mutant underg\u00e5ngens arvtagare :P <br /> Herosystem, DnD 3.5 and also 5ed , Exalted 2nd edition and Shadowrun<br /> I'm doing lot of alpha and beta testing in various MMO games or other online games such as LoL, Dota 2, Hearthstone or similar games and have done that since 10-12 years back now.<br /> <br /> In Exalted the Lunars are the one I'm most interested in and after that Dragon blooded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T06:29:04-08:00","id":1176762,"title":"","content":"I intend to actually post stuff now (after lurking for a while) so here goes...<br /> <br /> I'm RealityCheque (or RC) most places, except when some git took the name before me (or I was an idiot and lost the account, hello Twitter) in which case I'm usually known as Exalts for reasons that will be obvious to nobody but you lot. I'm from the UK, I work in IT, and I've been playing RPGs for 25 years (now I feel old) ever since we discovered carrying 3 books between us into school was a lot easier than several kilos of metal 40k models each.<br /> <br /> I've been playing Exalted since me and two friends found this cool looking book in a FLGS and went 3rds on it. 2 editions later, and it's our most played game since that day. We usually have a few games going on at once with different GMs and switch between them every 8-13 weeks, and it would be a safe bet that 2 out of the 3 are Exalted and that I'm running one of those games.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Roleplaying a dragonblooded 15 years ago accidentally helped me change my personality for the better... I literally would not be the person I am now without this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T08:19:00-08:00","id":1176772,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'll jump in!<br /> <br /> Simon here. Named after my Nuwisha character in our mix-and-match Werewolf game. As a Nuwisha Ghost-Dancer, Simon is quite capable of stepping across the Gauntlet reflexively. Even though he's rather weaker than the werewolves (and a were-lion!) around, he's no slouch in a fight - his Coyote's Tooth takes the form of a huge wrench, strikes across the Gauntlet, and can be used for grappling and judo/aikido throws. <br /> <br /> We keep winding up with games on-hold, because of changes in schedule, people moving, and so on. I've mentioned in passing a couple of times, that I'm hoping Ex3 can be our next game, and that I can prepare for it to accommodate people coming and going. We'll have up to 5 players plus storyteller, so quickness of turn resolution is vitally important to me. If we do go with Ex3, I'm just about certain we'll use the Momentum Exalted (see the forum thread) rules hack, because it's vastly faster.<br /> <br /> I sometimes write stories set in my campaigns. Some of them are to be further exposition, and some just come along naturally from after-inspiration during the week between play sessions. I'd love to write for a living and I keep wanting to submit some samples... but on the other hand I'd hate to have a fun hobby turn into work. First world problems!<br /> <br /> I have successfully made a player cry from a story reveal. I've given a player a week's insomnia over an upcoming decision. And I've had players dress up in costumes made especially after game ideas. Keeps me going!<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of Lunars. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Don't tell anybody, but I run game for a table full of furries)</span> I personally cast Celestials as peers of Solars, but with different roles, because turning everybody into &quot;and friends&quot; second-fiddles is crummy game writing. In 2nd Ed, I gave Sids a lot of extra leeway with astrology and resplendent destinies - basically letting them set up a pool of successes to draw from and some narrative oomph to change details of the scene if they'd done the arrangements ahead of time. Lunars automagically kept their inventory in Elsewhere and could choose what to have with them upon each shapeshift, and the Moonsilver Tattoos gained a lot of story leeway.<br /> <br /> For 3rd Ed, I was considering expanding on the Lunar-Elsewhere knack, by turning that Elsewhere into a Lair (a la Beast) with some detail and character to it. Their panoply of shapes and inventory would be hidden there, and sometimes a scene might take place there - maybe a conversation with the mind-shadow of someone the Lunar ate to gain knowledge from. Some part of my Lunar society would be working to build a network of Lair chambers in between Creation and the other realms, I think.... a bit more productive than humping beastmen at the edge of Creation. I was also considering having my game's Moonsilver Tattoos with a tree of Evocations, branching for each of the different Castes. So you'd start out as simply Shaping-resistant, but as your power and legend grew, you'd grow into the abilities of the phases of the moon - and be able to shift among them if you put the effort into being able to. Maybe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I haven't put together quite as much for how I want to do the other splats yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T01:42:35-08:00","id":1177200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1176772#post1176772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to write for a living and I keep wanting to submit some samples... but on the other hand I'd hate to have a fun hobby turn into work. First world problems!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what's keeping me from doing it too XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T09:27:31-08:00","id":1178456,"title":"","content":"Hi. I should introduce myself, since I have begun the inevitable slide from lurking to posting. History suggests this slide will continue. I'll try not to slide all the way to the insurmountable-walls-of-text phase I seem prone to.<br /> <br /> I'm an avid player/rules lawyer/system junkie. I love role-playing and role-playing games. I'm pretty new to Exalted, having only explored 2nd Edition through one-shots before diving into the most recent incarnation of Exalted. My general philosophy is that when playing, I want to have fun, I want to tell a good story, and I want everybody else at the table to have fun. Roughly in that order, because I'm selfish. Intelligent self-interest mostly herds me toward the second though, because that's how you get games to run better and longer.<br /> <br /> I'm a competent munchkin, but game-breaking tends to derail sessions, so I avoid it, and mostly use my rules-lawyering capabilities to try to make things run smoothly. Occasionally, the story is best served by doing something ludicrously effective/powerful/impactful, and if I can find a way to do it, that scratches two of my backs at once. (Oh god, what happened to this metaphor?)<br /> <br /> My current chronicle is has been running for 6-ish months, with a Circle of 4 Solars running amok under the benevolent guidance (heh) of our Storyteller.<br /> <br /> As is my wont, I've read the entire Core book and memorized fair chunks of it, and already have half a dozen character concepts brewing in the back of my head that I'll likely never get to play, since my Presence-Supernal Zenith, Defiant Clarity of Jade, doesn't show any signs of retiring from her campaign to rule all of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","name":"Catastronaut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T18:24:02-08:00","id":1180563,"title":"","content":"Hello, everyone! Long time listener, first time caller here. Decided it was time to end my commitment to lurking charms and finally start posting, so I figured I would introduce myself.<br /> <br /> I've been gaming on both sides of the table for years but 3rd edition is my first real experience with Exalted; I made one 2.5 character (a Twilight sorcerer with the teaching charms) but never actually got to play her. Playing in a 3rd edition campaign someone else was running hooked me, though, and I've been a fan since.<br /> <br /> I've actually built significantly more characters than I've played because I really enjoy the process of building characters, fiddly XP-saving math included! I'm terrible at homebrewing stuff, though, so Arms was a very welcome addition to my library. Currently very excited for What Fire Has Wrought so I can bring my Stormcaller/Mela's Coil-wielding Nellens sorcerer to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2265-retrokinesis","name":"Retrokinesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2265_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T06:54:05-08:00","id":1183250,"title":"","content":"I'm orukan, been lurking in here for a few months and finally decided to join a few days ago. Been playing exalted since first edition and liking the 3rd one so far. Never been a big fan of DnD because of number crunching and whatnot. I prefer RP over power playing, though I do love myself a good fight once in a while. I hail from the frigid northlands of little Canadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23809-orukan","name":"Orukan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T10:16:40-08:00","id":1183628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orukan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1183250#post1183250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm orukan, been lurking in here for a few months and finally decided to join a few days ago. Been playing exalted since first edition and liking the 3rd one so far. Never been a big fan of DnD because of number crunching and whatnot. I prefer RP over power playing, though I do love myself a good fight once in a while. I hail from the frigid northlands of little Canadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome!<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to hear how your actual play deals with Ex3's crunch, sometime!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T22:01:06-08:00","id":1186178,"title":"","content":"Hello to all. I've been an Exalted fan for a few years now, having gotten into it about a year or so before 3E dropped. D&amp;D was my gateway drug to tabletop RPG's, but I've played a lot of other systems too. The friends that I play with IRL are still mostly interested in D&amp;D, but I'm probably going to run an Exalted game for them soon enough. I hail from Terra Australis, on the eastern coast.<br /> <br /> I found myself making an account here when I realised I was spending more and more time lurking on these forums in the past few weeks while waiting for news of Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23881-lastchronicler","name":"LastChronicler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T21:57:56-08:00","id":1191838,"title":"","content":"Hi , user name tahu1809 hear. I've been interested in Exalted for a few years now. Little bit of funny background for me, I bought the core book for second edition back in summer of 2012. I.e around the time the last books for second edition was published. What got me into Exalted in the first place? The chapter comics. Well and the fanfiction Glorious shotgun Princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23746-tahu1809","name":"tahu1809","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:18:54-07:00","id":1202472,"title":"","content":"Well, I signed up and pretty much immediately moved house, so I hadn't gotten an opportunity to post much before we lost internet access for a fortnight. But that's sorted now so without further ado:<br /> <br /> Hi everyone. I'm from Brisbane, Australia. I've been playing Exalted since 2nd ed. I'm currently running a 2.5e Abyssals game in a modern version of Creation (I should probably say Abyssals/Solars game at this point since two of my PCs have gone and redeemed). That's been ongoing for three years now. Limited 3rd Ed play under my belt, but not for lack of enthusiasm. Looking forward to running it in the future, but I'm not about to do that while my other campaign is ongoing, and no one else in my group has volunteered to run it yet. <br /> <br /> I play a diverse range of systems since one of my gaming groups rotates GMs regularly and everyone has their favourite. But Exalted is the game that has most captured my imagination, chiefly because I fell head first into its setting and fell in love. <br /> <br /> I'll see you all around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:11:46-07:00","id":1204249,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Dex Davican. I was a 2E homebrew writer and became an Ex3 freelance writer. I'm a mental health professional, I'm an ST far more often than I am a player, and Homestuck might be my favorite single piece of media. I began the first Ask the Unconquered Sun thread, but lost it all when the forum changed over, which is surprisingly sad. I was also @malfeas on Twitter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T03:37:22-07:00","id":1207922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1204249#post1204249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm Dex Davican. I was a 2E homebrew writer and became an Ex3 freelance writer. I'm a mental health professional, I'm an ST far more often than I am a player, and Homestuck might be my favorite single piece of media. I began the first Ask the Unconquered Sun thread, but lost it all when the forum changed over, which is surprisingly sad. I was also @malfeas on Twitter.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're also, without exaggeration or dishonesty, the most creative man <i>ever to have lived.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T12:52:59-07:00","id":1209359,"title":"","content":"Hello! I've been interested in Exalted, but most of my IRL gaming buddies either default to D&amp;D or 'whatever Stareyes wants to run', and I have limited ability to ST any more -- I teach astronomy at our local university, and it turns out planning classes eats up a lot of my creative planning time and energy. (My job also means that I can nerd out about how stars would appear on a flat world, what the implications are for a Moon whose phase can be due to 'deity got bored', or the details of a calendar system.)<br /> <br /> So, looking forward to lurking around in the forum and at least talking setting, even if I haven't sunk my teeth into the crunchy bits too deeply yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24133-stareyes","name":"Stareyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T17:18:47-07:00","id":1213602,"title":"","content":"Hi! I'm a new-ish fan of Exalted. I've known about it since 2e but I couldn't properly get into until 3e came out. I dont have much experience but I'm willing to learn anything new.<br /> <br /> I backed the latest KS and had a lot of fun reading about DBs being themselves. I'll probably be an active participant in conversations here, and probably ST a game or two sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24165-parabola","name":"Parabola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T17:25:51-07:00","id":1213605,"title":"","content":"Deleted, because posted in wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","name":"Sequal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4862_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T06:29:47-07:00","id":1216079,"title":"","content":"Hello all! My name is Charles. I'd say I'm fairly new to Exalted. I did a lot of PBP for second edition with my friends, but I never sank too deeply into the lore and world and whatnot. Exalted is probably the best fantasy RPG of all time, and I'm currently trying to convince my Starfinder group to make the jump.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I am one of three hosts of premiere weekly Exalted podcast, The Deliberative Podcast. Check us out on iTunes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T07:26:41-07:00","id":1219627,"title":"","content":"Hi everybody!<br /> I used to be on the old forum just a little bit, and decided to get back into posting recently. I've been with Exalted since reading the 1st edition Core book, and have the 3rd core and WFHW kickstarted. I'm trying to get an Exalted group together in my hometown area that matches my odd schedule<br /> <br /> I hope to share lots of fun ideas here and read plenty more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T11:32:32-07:00","id":1225936,"title":"","content":"Hello ^^<br /> <br /> longtime lurker, longtime player, recent ST, only recently posting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T19:16:36-07:00","id":1229706,"title":"","content":"Hello! I am a low-level civil servant in the US government, recently out of college and a big fan of Exalted. I really like the setting and I'm super excited for all the new lore coming out in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24333-electronsutra","name":"ElectronSutra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24333_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T03:43:14-07:00","id":1231063,"title":"","content":"Woops, should probably do this thing.<br /> <br /> Hello! I live in New Zealand, I'm a graphic designer by trade and I've played Exalted since early first edition. I used to play in the official White Wolf online game set on some island called Jade. That was a super weird game and some people got angry with each other. I also helped run a rebel break-away online game set in a made up eastern location called Rinmarg, which had (very slightly) less online arguments. The lesson here is don't run large online games.<br /> <br /> Me and my buds play a variety of games every week like Call of Cthulhu and Gloomhaven and a zillion boardgames and once the Dragon Blooded book is officially out I'll be running us an Exalted game, my first time with 3rd edition. Chur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T02:01:28-07:00","id":1231545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1231063#post1231063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woops, should probably do this thing.<br /> <br /> Hello! I live in New Zealand, I'm a graphic designer by trade and I've played Exalted since early first edition. I used to play in the official White Wolf online game set on some island called Jade. That was a super weird game and some people got angry with each other. I also helped run a rebel break-away online game set in a made up eastern location called Rinmarg, which had (very slightly) less online arguments. The lesson here is don't run large online games.<br /> <br /> Me and my buds play a variety of games every week like Call of Cthulhu and Gloomhaven and a zillion boardgames and once the Dragon Blooded book is officially out I'll be running us an Exalted game, my first time with 3rd edition. Chur.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welcome back <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1079\" data-vbnamecard=\"1079\">Megapope</a>! It is awesome to see a familiar face posting here from the old days. I played in both Jade and Rinmarg. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T05:40:55-07:00","id":1234919,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Inertial Frame (see, it even says so on the left sidebar!). The name's a physics thing, a frame of reference for moving objects.<br /> <br /> I'm very new to Exalted rules, so much so I don't have any of the books yet, but I'm intrigued by the setting and system so far based on what I've read here. I started gaming around 30 years (!) ago with GURPS, but the first game I had a full time group for was AD&amp;D 2nd ed. I knew a playtester of Vampire back in the early 90's, which drew me to (classic) World of Darkness. Right now I playing in a (fairly house ruled) Vampire game and running a (n excessively homebrewed) Vampire variant. If I had the money, I'd probably jump into Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:21:38-07:00","id":1238618,"title":"","content":"Suppose I should introduce myself as I've made a couple of posts already.<br /> <br /> Heya! I'm a Finnish roleplayer/ GM, who got into the Exalted at the twilight of the Second edition. Back then I tried to run a campaign (Solars, one Infernal), which crashed as my group did not like the game enough to learn the rules. I came back, when 3rd edition launched and am now a happy player in a Solar campaign - and soon in a DB campaign too! My favourite type of Exalted are the Sidereals (tho Infernals come close).<br /> <br /> I started playing RPG's around the time I got too old for make-believe, tho I've actively played Pen&amp;Paper only since 2010. My first tabletop RPG's were GMing Call of Cthulhu and Rogue Trader. Nowadays I don't like to stick to one system so I play quite a lot of different games, like Savage Worlds, Blades in the Dark, ODnD, DnD4 and Night's Black Agents. And those are just the one's I actively play in addition to Exalted at the moment. I like homebrewing, but don't like numbers (which is kinda a bad match, I know). At the moment I have two artifacts and a martial art on the anvil, which I'll post here, when they're ready-ish. When playing a game, I tend to get interested in what the developers intended for the game - which I usually bend enough that they meet with what I want to run.<br /> I consider myself very lucky to live in a place, where I can generally choose to play and run games how I want.<br /> <br /> As a person I have MoA degree in Literature with a teacher's qualifications. I'm currently having a leap year (read: mandatory civil service), which I'm using to game and ponder, whether I should pursue a PhD or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","user":"Taleksi","date":".  Gah, swatted a typo! 07-25-2018, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T20:28:11-07:00","id":1242590,"title":"","content":"Hello. I am Malozing, and my friends call me Mal for short. I've started playing DnD 3.5 when I was 15 and played my first Exalted game in college. I am currently playing my first E3 game over on the GitP Forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Games I am currently playing in:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?594693-The-Convergence-of-Sky-An-Exalted-campaign\" target=\"_blank\">The Convergence of Sky (Exalted 3e)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?543906-The-Lotus-Blossoms!\" target=\"_blank\">The Lotus Blossoms! (Exalted 3e)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?584663-The-Lotus-Blossoms!-Volume-II\" target=\"_blank\">The Lotus Blossoms! Vol II (Exalted 3e)</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24467-malozing","name":"Malozing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T13:34:13-07:00","id":1258018,"title":"","content":"Wow, occurs to me I've never actually introduced myself here before...<br /> <br /> Hi, I go by Hand-of-Omega (Doctor Who reference if you're curious), and I've been into White Wolf since college in the 90s, when I was a huge fan of the original World of Darkness, esp. the Eastern-themed Year of the Lotus line. I was really excited to learn the folks behind that were starting a new game based on the pre-history of the WoD! Turned out that connection was highly exaggerated, but by that point I didn't care, I was hooked and never looked back. <br /> <br /> Finding Exalted was probably <i>the</i> greatest joy of my gaming life; rarely having the time and opportunity to actually <i>play</i> it would be the saddest part of it. At this point, I'm pretty resigned to just collecting the books and enjoying the world of Creation in my own head...and this forum! I've been with Exalted from the start and have been through about three forum reboots on this site. Every now and then, I take a month or so off, but I think this last hiatus (which was due to family issues) was my longest yet. <br /> <br /> I actually got tired of waiting for Third Edition books (beyond the two released of course), so when other stuff demanded my time, I just kinda let Exalted go for awhile. Recently, however, I found myself digging out my old collection, and realized just how much I missed reading through them and discussing stuff here with you good folks. So, I thought it time I circle back around, this time for the foreseeable future! I see there's a lot of new names here, so I hope we can all have fun with 3E!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T11:08:26-07:00","id":1263097,"title":"","content":"Hello. A ST in his late thirties, mostly with experience in warhammer, D&amp;D and oWoD, now trying his hand at Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T13:33:18-07:00","id":1263121,"title":"","content":"Hi ^^)/<br /> <br /> I'm RosePlancton (Rose is okay ^^ ) a 25 years college student from France and a visual artist (doing mostly drawings, clay sculpting and computer graphics).I'm GMing since I'm 12, playing lots of things with my numerous family like The Dark Eye, DnD 3.5, WoD (old and new), Pathfinder, Feng Shui, Qin and lots of &quot;custom rulesets&quot;.<br /> I discovered Exalted and Aberrant in 2017 and I became a groupie of both but after half a year playing Exalted I had to stop a month ago because of health issues.<br /> I'm still in love with its setting and I've been lurking here for a long time, reading lots of cool conversations about the setting and seeing lots of points of view about the game, its lore and how others are playing it. ^^<br /> I'm used to look at things from afar even on the internet but sometimes it's fun to not just be an observer. Soooo I'm here and talking (writing ?). X)<br /> <br /> <br /> I've talked about me being a visual artist because despite the fact that I don't want to GM this game for now because of my health and my time consuming double degree, I'm still inspired a lot by it and it makes me want to draw and paint lots of Exalted inspired things. ^^<br /> I don't know, maybe I'll post some things I'm working on. X)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T07:00:15-08:00","id":1271970,"title":"","content":"Howdy,<br /> <br /> I go by VVolf on the interwebs have been playing traditional pen and paper RPGs since 2005 or so, starting with D&amp;D 4th Ed (Yes, there are people who enjoyed 4E) and first got introduced to Exalted about a year ago. Between then I've played Pathfinder, Dresden Files RPG (Fate system), Mouse Guard RPG (Burning Wheel system), Ironclaw (Cardinal system), and probably some more that I can't think of at the moment...<br /> <br /> When forced to RP as a responsible adult, I work as a web developer and live in College Station, Texas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24875-vvolf","name":"VVolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24875_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:58:55-07:00","id":1299063,"title":"","content":"Hello, happy to join these forums. I had been following them for a long time but now that I have more time and decided to register and participate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:51:32-07:00","id":1299250,"title":"","content":"Hi. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I choose to be known as Aspiring Hopeful Hero, because being a hero is something worth aspiring towards.<br /> I am currently a student in Norway.<br /> <br /> I accidentally posted my own introduction thread because I did not see this one. -.-<br /> <br /> I have known about Exalted for a while, but I have never had the opportunity to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25187-aspiring-hopeful-hero","name":"Aspiring Hopeful Hero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T11:12:52-07:00","id":1309232,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I'm a programmer in his 30s. A friend introduced me to Exalted 2 years ago and I've been hooked ever since.<br /> <br /> What I love most about the 3E is that it encourages creating custom Charms and custom Artifacts/Evocations, which I love coming up with.<br /> <br /> So of course I am very much looking forward to the Exigents book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T02:10:40-07:00","id":1309392,"title":"","content":"I can finally write here.<br /> <br /> Hello there. Long time lurker here. I decided to start an account since with the arrive of the Lunars I felt the time was right (I have a weakness for trickster characters and the Lunars are perfect for the part). So, here I am.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone that lurk around Spacebattle know me already, right <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> ?<br /> <br /> Well, that's it. Oh, another thing: if you see me make some grammatical error, please have patience. Secondary language and all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T06:08:59-07:00","id":1309422,"title":"","content":"Hi, welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T06:53:59-07:00","id":1317553,"title":"","content":"Longtime lurker for all things Exalted and CWoD, and devourer of lore in many forms and tastes. For Revised Editions for CWoD and Exalted, I've got a fair amount of info and speculation all over the place. Like.. A lot of underlying thoughts; Get me going on Ex2E motonic theories, and I could possibly go for a while.<br /> <br /> I ran an Exalted Modern game for the better part of ten years, though, sadly, it wound up falling by the wayside after my wife passed away. I've got a setting project or two in the works, still working on 'em.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm Sye. Field Service Technician in Ohio. Generally, I install VoIP phones and teach tech-illiterate the various uses the app can do. I also pull ethernet cable, and various things in association with infrastructure. IT's my wheelhouse, and I like to think I'm a pretty solid generalist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24956-the_sye","name":"The_Sye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24956_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T13:04:27-07:00","id":1317662,"title":"","content":"Sye, if you don't mind my asking, what part of Ohio?<br /> Also, will you be attending Origins this week?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T17:19:42-07:00","id":1321561,"title":"","content":"Hey, everyone! I'm a gamer in the Allentown area; I play mostly online these days but have been with Exalted since early 2nd ed when I fell in love with it and never left. Currently I'm playing a campaign in the west as a Twilight based on a combination of Luffy from One Piece and How I Got Reincarnated as a Slime. Glad to be here after lurking for so long!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25409-cobra","name":"Cobra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T05:05:25-07:00","id":1333807,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone !<br /> <br /> So I have been playing Exalted since 2011, it also was my first campaign and my first character. That year I also did my debuts as a GM. Since then I have been much more a GM than a PC but it's alright, I enjoy it very much and it seems that my players do too.<br /> <br /> I have GMed several kind of Exalted but mortals too. Had even 2 campaigns with mortals on 3ed which is pretty funky (so close to death every fight ^^). And I'm looking forward to launch a solar campaign IRL and maybe a Dragon-Blooded campaign online. As such I'm coming here for 2nd opinions on some ideas and a few rules clarification, as well as contributing as much as I can to your ideas too !<br /> <br /> At this point I should say that I'm French and I'm pretty sure my players don't come here. And if they want surprises they should stay away too ^^ But don't worry the Exalted gospel is spreading here too, one exaltation at a time.<br /> <br /> Glad to join you all ! See you around <br /> (roll [Perception+Awareness] please)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","user":"Crop Weaver","date":". 09-04-2019, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","name":"Crop Weaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:30:31-08:00","id":1347498,"title":"","content":"Hi I'm Chausse.<br /> <br /> I didn't notice this topic before so I decided to make a brief introduction when I saw it.<br /> <br /> I'm a French student that just started a Ph.D in Cryptography. I've been lurking and answering on this forum for about a year or so. I've done 3-4 campaigns of Exalted with my closest friends since I first discovered it about 3 years ago, and since then I just can't stop playing Exalted. I really appreciate the support of the community concerning my (numerous) questions about Exalted.<br /> <br /> Please excuse my english that is sometimes quite poor or litteral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:07:00-07:00","id":1380900,"title":"","content":"Hi I'm Qendi, and I still don't know how I have missed this thread.<br /> <br /> I've been with Exalted for the last 12-ish years, including being involved in publishing Polish edition of Ealted 2nd. Currently living in Paris suburbs (les salutations <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> and pardon for my google translate level French) and teaching in International School when I'm not dabbling with RPGs.<br /> <br /> I've been running mainly 2nd edition with Solars and Dragon-Bloodeds with a huge break when the 3rd edition came out, to be back to storytelling now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T07:42:08-07:00","id":1380938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1380900#post1380900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (les salutations <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> and pardon for my google translate level French)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi ! Nice to meet you ! Quick question if I may : I understand from your post you are not French, where are you from ? Anyway a pleasure to know someone with good taste is from not afar <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:19:23-07:00","id":1394787,"title":"","content":"Hi all, been playing Exalted since 1st edition, and it's my favorite TTRPG of all time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My group generally still plays 2.5e, though with a generous helping of the cool new stuff from 3e that we like (e.g., sorcery rules, Evocations, Exigents, some of the new setting features, etc.) while ignoring the stuff we don't (e.g., Liminals, Getimians, and that <i>horridly </i>overcomplicated combat engine).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T17:22:38-07:00","id":1395184,"title":"","content":"I'm Jimborg. This is more of a re-introduction than anything. I used to be fairly active on the old White Wolf forums before they got moved over here. I was a big fan of Exalted 2ed and, I needed some time before I could accept Exalted 3ed. But I've skimmed the Core and Dragon Blooded and I'm fairly happy with what I've seen so far, though Sidereals are my favorite splat and I can't wait for them to be published.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:26:12-07:00","id":1397948,"title":"","content":"So I thought I had done this when I first became a member, but nope. So hi, I'm Arkayriel known to my family as Tony and called much meaner names by my friends. I've been playing pen and paper rpgs for 20 years now starting with 2nd ed DnD. I started playing Exalted in the last couple of years of 1st edition and played many games in 2nd and am now playing 3rd. My favorite splat is still and always will be solars, but I'm really loving what they've done to dragon-bloods and lunars. I'm looking forward to many discussions with you all, cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:38:39-07:00","id":1414731,"title":"","content":"edit: this is not the ask a dev thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23840-teal-tara","name":"Teal Tara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T14:32:05-08:00","id":1423372,"title":"","content":"Hello there, long-time lurker both here and from the old forums before the move to Onyx Path years ago. I've played my share of the original WoD games, but my favorite games were from the more heroic and epic lines like Aberrant, Exalted and Scion. I've dipped into Exalted since 1st edition but the majority of my games ran with the 2nd edition. After years playing it, though, I felt a bit burnt out and shifted my attention elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Exalted 3e is pretty much an entirely different beast and got me hooked right back into the setting, which now feels familiar but new at the same time, and is the main reason why I'm leaving my old status as 'eternal lurker'. I really like the changes to some 'canon characters' like Mnemon and Lilith, and though I kind of miss Magitech, I understand and approve the decision to abandon it and make artifacts unique as they are now.<br /> <br /> So basically just an old time Exalted geek speaking up for the first time. Nothing new or special to see here. Thank you for your time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26546-legendarycontradiction","name":"LegendaryContradiction","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26546_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T00:46:56-08:00","id":1423490,"title":"","content":"I have, after many moons, gained the ability to post, and so decided to introduce myself. Hi! I'm Elenian. I've been lurking on this forum for... quite a while, though only now have I 1) actually created an account and 2) started a (Dragonblooded) Exalted game. In my day job I'm an academic who studies the history of demons in European philosophy, and so of course I have an affinity for all things demonic in games, too.<br /> <br /> Greetings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26536-elenian","name":"Elenian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T02:10:14-08:00","id":1426662,"title":"","content":"Hey team. I am zennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 11-30-2020, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T20:02:13-08:00","id":1427516,"title":"","content":"joshopotamus of the central texas region. Been playing exalted since maybe 2008-2009. Since then its become my favorite of all rpgs and i've recently come back to see how much further along 3rd ed has developed. Just dropped a mint on splat books and charm cards because i fucking love this game and plan to force some local friends to play with me. I also study southern chinese kung fu which often informs the games i write and play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T11:41:52-08:00","id":1427732,"title":"","content":"Hi, I\u2019m Mr Croquemitaine !<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a formal french student in literatures and work for an independant publisher who produce political and social sciences books, also launching my own publishing house in the coming year.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been introduce to this awesome game that is exalted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a>, who was the ST for our first campaign. Since then I\u2019ve been lurking around and I have posted one time, long ago.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think I\u2019m gonna post a little more here so I\u2019m introducing myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry for my english, I will do my best !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13634-mrcroquemitaine","name":"MrCroquemitaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13634_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T05:43:06-08:00","id":1428079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrCroquemitaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1427732#post1427732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I\u2019m Mr Croquemitaine !<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a formal french student in literatures and work for an independant publisher who produce political and social sciences books, also launching my own publishing house in the coming year.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been introduce to this awesome game that is exalted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a>, who was the ST for our first campaign. Since then I\u2019ve been lurking around and I have posted one time, long ago.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think I\u2019m gonna post a little more here so I\u2019m introducing myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry for my english, I will do my best !</div> </div> </div> </div>Protip : He looks like his avatar <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T07:21:26-08:00","id":1429357,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm Kate, co-founding member of RPGClinic, or as folks around here might remember us from, ExalTwitch. We've come a very very long way from balancing old webcams on board game boxes five years ago, and are gearing up to return to the world of Exalted. This time we're going to be Dragon-Blooded, so I'm excited to be browsing the various threads on the matter.<br /> <br /> Other stuff about me? I'm a stage manager by profession, so I've had quite a bit of spare time on my hands in 2020. I'm very interested in stream technology (I just discovered Up Deck this year and it's helped us up our game significantly) and lately have been having a blast discovering a lot of one-shot TTRPG systems (because not every game's rulebook needs to be classified as a weapon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). <br /> <br /> I'm also quite (patiently) hyped for Essence, but know that is many months away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Kate, co-founding member of <a href=\"http://www.rpgclinic.com\" target=\"_blank\">RPGClinic</a> (known for <i>ExalTwitch</i> and <i>Changeling: The Streaming</i>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26603-zen_r0b0","name":"Zen_r0b0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T20:56:02-07:00","id":1440682,"title":"","content":"I'm Rodell, fairly active member of the Exalted subreddit and I recently started an Exalted podcast. I run two games and I'm a player in two others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26740-wandering-mendicant","name":"Wandering Mendicant","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"0"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T16:55:20-08:00","id":1471110,"title":"","content":"Hello! I'm Ignepkt. I've been consistently playing RPGs for about 7 or 8 years, possibly longer depending on how exactly one counts it. I started with D&amp;D 3.5, then played a lot of Pathfinder 1 with my friends. We eventually moved on to D&amp;D 5e. There's also a some not-quite-D&amp;D that I like, such as Ultraviolet Grasslands and Stars Without Number.<br /> <br /> I first became aware of Exalted around, oh, 2013-ish, possibly earlier, when my brother got the first edition rulebook. I started actually playing it sometime in early to mid 2020, I want to say, when a friend of mine asked if I wanted to GM a solo campaign for him in 2nd edition. I said yes. The specifics of the solo campaign have changed over time, starting as a Northern Zenith Solar and taking a brief interlude for an Eastern No Moon Lunar. Both of those iterations of the campaign were eventually put to bed and we've settled on a Southern Malefactor Infernal intent on wresting Gem from the Despot, then later conquering Malfeas and the South.<br /> <br /> I look forward to my time here with everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27223-ignepkt","name":"Ignepkt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"0"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T00:47:38-08:00","id":1474264,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm CT Phipps and starting my first Exalted campaign soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:36:25-07:00","id":1491038,"title":"","content":"Hi all, I am Pierre (in english peter). I live somewhere in europa in a country named France. I began to play to RPG for a long time and a long time ago, since I had 10 years old. Actually I have more than 40 years.I have actually play to exalted version 3.0 two time, so I know a little bit the rules, but I am not an expert. So if you have a place to a new player it will be cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27547-the-true","name":"THE TRUE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T08:08:37-07:00","id":1491477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=1474264#post1474264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I'm CT Phipps and starting my first Exalted campaign soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hy CT Phipps,<br /> When you stared your frst campaign, then I will be interested to be one of your players, if you are interested<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27547-the-true","name":"THE TRUE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T08:09:07-07:00","id":1491478,"title":"","content":"a mistake. YesI have answer two time with the same message <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27547-the-true","name":"THE TRUE","avatar":"data:imag